ompression techniques appear could double triple transponder capacity using existing near term transponders one the significant possible changes the market was identified the arrival new launch vehicles including russian launch systems but arianespace predicts that the long term investors purchasing launch services are looking for the best trade off between launch service quality and price and that russian and other new launch services will have prove out their capabilities and service quality and their market penetration will minimal commentary ariane releases their market surveys annually and reported their prior market survey past issue csn sti comparing the two surveys there aren outstanding differences the numbers the most notable change the consideration new data compression techniques reducing the demand for new physical transponders orbit note that contrast some predictions demand for space based communications transponders appears remain strong while fiber optic lines are making substantial inroads into the established point point telecommunications markets growing demand for telecommunications services world wide and for point multipoint broadcast services have prevented decrease space transponder demand fiberoptic cables provide higher capability service but only from established point established point establish fiberoptic link necessary install cable between the points and while there are improved network solutions installing large network distributed fiberoptic links can cost millions billions dollars for broadcast services where there not existing ground network structure satellites still offer the most cost effective solution and new services are required into new region cheaper install small satellite link costing only few tens thousands dollars and tie into the existing global satellite network this allows rapid growth new satellite services and has kept demand high the replacement market for fiberoptics growing well since demand grows between the 