n since valid abort order was given under agreed launch constraint rules and was not obeyed leading the investigation the national transportation safety board ntsb with support from nasa osc and the air force this investigation marks the first time ntsb has taken the lead incident involving space launch according the ntsb their investigation will take about months and primarily looking lines authority communications links and safety procedures used the launch commentary this the first time that the ntsb has led investigation into space launch their leadership was requested the department commerce office commercial space transportation who had licensed the commercial launch the time writing this column some the initial investigations have been concluded and some the results are starting leak out into the trade press apparently four different communications channels were use during the test after the abort destruct receiver stopped responding the nasa test director and range controller the mission control room wallops island gave abort orders about minute before the launch according the mission rules this should have stopped the launch somehow the osc test conductor ordered the abort reversed and the nasa communicator the net relayed that order the carrying the pegasus about seconds before launch differing explainations exactly how this happened are proposed with the best set being that clear lines communications and clear definition the responsibilities the mission control team and understanding the mission rules were not established before the launch see more and more commercial launches more these procedural issues are going crop and will have resolved this case interesting because the first time the ntsb has been called investigate commercial launch problem they with commercial aircraft problems think this problem will turn out primarily problems with procedures and communications and will cleared with issuance guidelines how launch communications should set and h