14 |text from mhollowa sunysb edu michael holloway subject transplant recipients newsletter april dinternational newsletter april nntp posting host engws5 sunysb edu organization state university new york stony brook lines 180 this will the first monthly postings the newsletter the long island chapter the transplant recipients international organization trio unfortunately was unable post before the date this month meeting posting anyway and posting world wide instead regional the hopes that some the information may useful illustrative also hope can used example and inspiration for the posting other newsletters and data related organ transplantation and donation mike transplant recipients international organization long island chapter box 922 huntington 11743 0922 newsletter 516 421 3258 april 1993 volume next meeting the next meeting wednesday april the knights columbus emerald manor 517 uniondale avenue uniondale our guest speaker will lewis teperman teperman trained pittsburgh under starzl and now the assistant director the liver transplant program new york university medical center teperman will discuss current trends transplantation and treatment and will answer questions long time friend trio surgeon many our members and always gracious and delightful guest sure very informative interesting and engaging evening our hospitality committee bette and vito suglia and jim spence will well prepared and last the weather should cooperative hope see very large gathering welcome teperman wednesday april uniondale last meeting has been noted here before that the long island chapter trio has extraordinary power predicting bad weather being able forecast rain sleet and snow fully month advance weatherman can match this time not only scored again but were also able disable the long island railroad making travel really difficult none the less many braved the snow and had interesting meeting and good conversation our scheduled speaker mrs elizabeth linnehan professional nutritionist had family emergency and was not able attend she hope she will with the fall discuss diet and medications however jennifer friedman image consultant and sister liver transplant recipient was kind enough step very short notice friedman gave lot good advice about choosing clothes and makeup even bit for men help look well and healthy and minimize some the cosmetic effects some the medicine and drugs take are most grateful jennifer and thank her for entertaining evening annual meeting addition welcoming teperman the april meeting also the annual meeting the chapter this the official notice the meeting required our laws the main purpose the meeting review the past year solicit member views and ideas for better ways meet their needs and elect members the board directors for the coming two year term the nominating committee has prepared the following slate for the board anne liver recipient and don treffeisen robert heart recipient and eulene smith vito kidney recipient and bette suglia kay grenzig liver recipient jan schichtel kidney recipient larry juliano kidney recipient david bekofsky director public education litp those remaining the board for another year are robert carroll liver kidney pancreas recipient jerry kidney recipient and jeanne eichhorn ron kidney donor and marie healy peter smith bone marrow recipient patricia ann yankus kidney and pancreas recipient walter ruzak kidney recipient this may seem big board but many hands make light work and with our various medical uncertainties good have backups for all the jobs the board therefore addition the slate being presented for voting nominations will also accepted from the floor there set number board members and there plenty work addition brief treasurer and membership reports will given and the floor will open for any new business suggestions comments anyone would like bring will keep the formal meeting short that can spend the majority the time with teperman future meetings remember the scheduled guests for the rest the year may peter shaprio chief psychiatry columbia presbyterian medical center june felix rappaport director the stony brook kidney transplant program plan being with the second wednesday each month notdaw the week april national organ and tissue donor awareness week notdaw while are planning news releases speaking engagements and meetings with supervisors gullata and gaffney have decided not have our softball game because two year experience with miserable weather all can help spread the word donor awareness however have found effective ask your pastor rabbi publish letter announcement the parish bulletin allow you address the congregation include mention the gift life his sermon attached this newsletter sample letter and fact sheet you can use thank you starzl honored the long island chapter the american liver foundation will hold its annual auction and dinner dance may 7th the fountainbleu jericho turnpike jericho thomas starzl will the honored guest tickets are person and are going fast you like meet starzl call anne treffeisen 516 421 3258 for details membership news congratulations reese received his heart transplant pittsburgh after waiting years home and doing well after only days hospital arthur michaels liver recipient planning run the boston marathon april what fantastic proof that transplantation works hope the national press notices bob mccormack after persistent bout with infection had his transplanted kidney removed home now back dialysis and feeling better nicole healy kidney recipient and daughter ron and marie spent the past several weeks hospital miami with problems encountered vacation marie has been with her florida they are back new york where nicole treatment will continue wish nicole speedy recovery kay grenzig liver recipient mending now after bad fall that resulted broken arm and broken leg kay candidate for the board need her well soon and best wishes all coming out the flu was tough winter for many but the tulips are just under the snow see you wednesday april uniondale lewis teperman
5 |text from peter hansen pgmoffc bnr subject help internal hds mac xxdate tue apr gmt nntp posting host bcarm382 organization bnr useragent nuntius 1d17 lines article 1993apr1 054820 3942 siemens kurt netzer kurt siemens writes possible install 2nd 100 mac with qunatum can pin cable with connectors for the internal motherboard scsi connector and the scsi connectors the first terminated the second will whats about the power supply where can connect amp connector supply very possible connect another internal hard disk any macintosh you can find the space put have iisi that came with quantum meg drive when ran into space problems slapped another meg quantum that had sitting shelf here what did first off was concerned about space since both drives are quantum quarter height drives finally decided that the logical place for them was stacked one upon the other fine they fit snugly have not had problem with heat yet and these drives have been running together for over two months the next problem was connecting the drive you have spare internal hard disk power cable did then half your troubles are over just splice the extra cable that you get one square motherboard connector and two hard disk power connectors you don have spare cable you will have buy the wires and connectors which can found any good electronics store for about would suggest properly soldering heatshrinking the connections reduce the possibility shorts bad connections next you need ribbon cable connection again had spare hard disk ribbon cable and wanted careful case this didn word what did was purchase crimp pin cable connector that gave another male connector the middle spare cable the part cost again and easily attached with any good wood vice the theory behind using crimp connector that this doesn work original cable not damaged and can back the original setup having done all that couldn bothered check the dev notes for power consumption plugged and works like charm this day mac everything should work the same careful with the the drive and ensure that the terminating resistors both drives are intact did not try this without the terminating resistors but seemed logical that splitting the scsi chain that the signal should terminated all the ends let know you have any more questions peter hansen bell northern research pgmoffc bnr
