15 |text from baez guitar ucr edu john baez subject end the space age article galaxy 29034 organization university california riverside lines nntp posting host guitar ucr edu there interesting opinion piece the business section today times thursday april 1993 thought post stir some flame wars mean reasoned debate let preface saying that largely agree that the space age the romantic sense several decades ago over and that projects like the space station miss the point this time reading for example what new the weekly physics update get here the net clear that the romance the day lies the ever more fine grained manipulation matter which include biotechnology condensed matter physics with its spinoffs computer hardware and elsewhere and the amazing things people are doing with individual atoms these days large extent think the romance some people still have with space matter nostalgia feel sure that someday more precisely our mind children will spread across space unless wipe ourselves out but think that manned space exploration not what exciting about what can now anyway let quote some this article but not all space age glory fades from view micheal schrage writer consultant and research associate mit america space age won have suffer through the angst midlife crisis the reason that the space age already dead the technologies longer define our times and the public has grown weary the multibillion dollar celestial investments that yield minimal psychic economic rewards space exploration has mutated from central focuse america science and technology debate into peripheral issue speace not meaningful part the ongoing industrial competitiveness debate our technology infrastructure discussions even our defense conversion policy sure america should continue invest satellite technologies for telecommunications and remote sensing cheap deep space probes would nice too but the ideal space meaningful driver scientific and industrial innovation now dead before the change administrations would have been foolish write obituary for the space age the bush white house aggressively supported the space program and proposed spending well over billion build space station freedom alone even proposed budget cuts other science and technology domains office management and budget director richard darman was outspoken public champion big ticket space expenditures the reality that much the civilian space program from the shuttle the hubble telescope the space station was poorly conceived and unimpressively implemented did not seem matter much political inertia and nostalgic sense futurism not coherent vision cost effective sensibilities determined multibillion dollar space budgets indeed with few notable exceptions such voyager the post apollo era the story the gold plated porkification space exploration with programs and promises that delivered less for more and more while the clinton administration has kept the highly regarded daniel goldin administrator the national aeronautics and space administration seems clear that space exploration not being positioned either symbolic substantive centerpiece america technological prowess the space station budget has rightly been slashed space virtually ignored when the administration champions its competitiveness agenda wish this had happened years ago instead starting happen now says bruce murray caltech professor who ran nasa jet propulsion lab pasadena put off lot things shouldn have would rather see billion nasa doing well than billion one filled with white elephants
