e cider also have been implicated preliminary data from cdc year nationwide multicenter study revealed that when stools were routinely cultured for coli o157 that organism was isolated more frequently than shigella four participating hospitals and was isolated from all bloody stools higher rate than for any other pathogen infection with coli o157 often not recognized because most clinical laboratories not routinely culture stools for this organism hicnet medical newsletter page volume number april 1993 smac medium and many clinicians are unaware the spectrum illnesses associated with infection the usual clinical manifestations are diarrhea often bloody and abdominal cramps fever infrequent younger age groups and the elderly are highest risk for clinical manifestations and complications illness usually resolves after days but patients develop hus which characterized hemolytic anemia thrombocytopenia renal failure and death rate this report illustrates the difficulties recognizing community outbreaks coli o157 the absence routine surveillance despite the magnitude this outbreak the problem may not have been recognized three states the epidemiologic link had not been established washington clinical laboratories should routinely culture stool specimens from persons with bloody diarrhea hus for coli o157 using smac agar when infections with coli o157 are identified they should reported local health departments for further evaluation and necessary public health action prevent further cases coli o157 lives the intestines healthy cattle and can contaminate meat during slaughter cdc collaborating with the department agriculture food safety inspection service identify critical control points processing component program reduce the likelihood pathogens such coli o157 entering the meat supply because slaughtering practices can result contamination raw meat with pathogens and because the process grinding beef may transfer pathogens from the surface the meat the interior ground beef likely internally contaminated the optimal food protection practice cook ground beef thoroughly until the interior longer pink and the juices are clear this outbreak undercooking hamburger patties likely played important role the food and drug administration fda has issued interim recommendations increase the internal temperature for cooked hamburgers 155 fda personal communication 1993 regulatory actions stimulated the outbreak described this report and the recovery thousands contaminated patties before they could consumed emphasize the value rapid public health investigations outbreaks the public health impact and increasing frequency isolation this pathogen underscore the need for improved surveillance for infections caused coli o157 and for hus better define the epidemiology coli o157 references cdc preliminary report foodborne outbreak escherichia coli o157 infections from hamburgers western united states 1993 mmwr 1993 riley remis helgerson hemorrhagic colitis associated with rare escherichia coli serotype engl med 1983 308 681 hicnet medical newsletter page volume number april 1993 griffin tauxe the epidemiology infections caused escherichia coli o157 other enterohemorrhagic coli and the associated hemolytic uremic syndrome epidemiol rev 1991 griffin ostroff tauxe illnesses associated with escherichia coli o157 infections broad clinical spectrum ann intern med 1988 109 705 march ratnam latex agglutination test hicnet medical newsletter page volume number april 1993 use smokeless tobacco among adults united states 1991 source mmwr date apr 1993 consumption moist snuff and other smokeless tobacco products the united states almost tripled from 1972 through 1991 long term use smokeless tobacco associated with nicotine addiction and increased risk oral cancer the incidence which could increase young persons who currently use smokeless tobacco continue use these products frequently monitor trends the prevalence use smokeless tobacco products cdc 1991 national health interview survey health promotion and disease prevention supplement nhis hpdp collected information snuff and chewing tobacco use and smoking from representative sample the civilian noninstitutionalized population aged greater than equal years this report summarizes findings from this survey the 1991 nhis hpdp supplement asked have you used snuff least times your entire life and you use snuff now similar questions were asked about chewing tobacco use and cigarette smoking current users smokeless tobacco were defined those who reported snuff chewing tobacco use least times and who reported using snuff chewing tobacco the time the interview former users were defined those who reported having used snuff chewing tobacco least times and not using either the time the interview ever users smokeless tobacco included current and former users current smokers were defined those who reported smoking least 100 cigarettes and who were currently smoking and former smokers those who reported having smoked least 100 cigarettes and who were not smoking now ever smokers included current and former smokers data smokeless tobacco use were available for 732 persons aged greater than equal years and were adjusted for nonresponse and weighted provide national estimates confidence intervals cis were calculated using standard errors generated the software for survey data analysis sudaan 1991 estimated million adults were current users smokeless tobacco including million men and 533 000 women for all categories comparison the prevalence smokeless tobacco use was substantially higher among men for men the prevalence use was highest among those aged years table for women the prevalence was highest among those aged greater than equal years the prevalence smokeless tobacco use among men was highest among american indians alaskan natives and whites the prevalence among women was highest among american indians alaskan natives and blacks among both men and women prevalence smokeless tobacco us