g ssf lab module docking ports are added for the international partners labs taking the place the nodes ssf the shuttle can docked the station for day missions the orbiter would provide crew habitability eva capability international human tended add the nasda esa modules and add another power permanent human presence capability add 3rd power module the habitation module and acrv assured crew return vehicle option space station freedom derived the option team based larc and lead mike griffin this option looks alot like the existing ssf design which have all come know and love this option assumes lightweight external tank available for use all ssf assembly flights does option also the number flights computed for inclination orbit for both options and the build occurs six phases initial research capability reached after flights power transferred from the vehicle the orbiter spacelab when visits man tended capability griffin has not yet adopted non sexist language achieved after flights the lab deployed and solar power module provides power permanent human presence capability occurs after flights keeping one orbiter orbit use acrv sometimes there would two orbiters orbit the acrv and the second one that comes for logistics supply two fault tolerance capability achieved after flights with the addition 2nd power module another thermal control system radiator and more propulsion modules after flights the internationals are board more power the habitation module and acrv are added finish the assembly flights most the systems currently ssf are used this option with the exception the data management system which has major changes option single core launch station this the jsc lead option basically you take diameter cylinder that long slap space shuttle main engines the backside put nose cone the top attached regular shuttle external tank and regular set solid rocket motors and launch the can some key features are complete end end ground integration and checkout tangentially mounted fixed solar panels body mounted radiators which adds protection against micrometeroid orbital debris centerline docking ports one each end berthing ports single pressurized volume approximately 000 cubic feet twice the volume skylab floors center passageway between floors housekeeping power graceful degradation with failures power channels thermal loops dual environmental control life support system increased crew time for utilization micro thru out the core module
