8 |text from charlesw sail labs tek com charles wilson subject experience opinions sought diesel engines article sail 13600 organization tektronix inc beaverton lines article 91321 hydra gatech edu jkg jmp com writes apologies this faq there faq posting for this group infrequent reader rec autos can remember the market for used chevy suburban and have observed that prices for models with diesel engines run about 1000 2000 less than comparable models with gas engine there has reason for this yes there consumer confusion the early with the fuel crisis etc everyone wanted better fuel mileage diesel fuel was the cheapest fuel available and usually provides better mileage than comparable gasoline engines decided conver their 350 gas engine into diesel engine think was liter big mistake the engine was not redesigned but converted the engine could not handle the higher compression etc lots problems with these cars this thew big red flag the casual observer don buy diesel they are bad this was gross generalization ask yourself this question your livelihood depended driving lots would you use dependable undependable but cheaper the short run vehicle what greyhound busses have them trailer trucks even train locomotives are these gasoline engines they are diesel tractor trailer truck manufacturers provide 500 000 mile warrantee with they vehicles own diesel suburban the diesel great engine just keeps going was more expensive when new than the gasoline engine vehicle was the only problem with diesel engines that when they need rebuilt they are expensive gas 350 engine you will pay about 1000 for rebuild diesel about 2000 but then again the diesel engine lasts about twice long and gets about better mileage carburator for gasoline engine costs about 100 rebuild less rebuild the fuel injection pump diesel will cost about 500 more but then again you never need tune you looking rebuilt say you got great deal check see the fuel injection pump was rebuilt also good luck
