4 |text from whiles nswc navy mil william scott hiles x1568 subject tape drive problems reply whiles nswc navy mil organization naval surface warfare center dahlgren division lines article 489 ux1 cso uiuc edu husak ux1 cso uiuc edu stephen husak writes please reply via mail since this job related have colorado jumbo back system one places employment and has eaten two tapes winding the tape off the spool there easy fix the tape drive fried does simply need cleaning any and all comments will appreciated stephen husak what trying what trying say not trying tell you anything you didn know when you woke today depeche mode nothing music for the masses stephen husak husak ux1 cso uiuc edu univerisity illinois does all tapes were the two tapes that unwound the same type from the same batch the reason ask that bought some generic tapes that did this and found that the tape markers were not fully punched out and had closed the little marker hole was only few tapes set did you open the tape cartridge and put the tape back the reels you have not yet open removing the two screws the bottom the tape cartridge and snap the plastic shell away from the metal base you are pulling the tape through the assembly try not touch any more than you have you are doing look for couple little holes the tape these are the marker holes which let the tape drive know when the end the tape the holes are spaced couple inches apart best guess that the drive finds the first marker and then stops the second marker anyhow the tape has the holes then check see the mirror the tape clean the function the mirror detect the marker holes the tape drive shines light the mirror and has pickup the area where the reflection would come out when the hole goes the pickup detects the light that was allowed pass and knows when stop the mirror dirty out alighment unlikely since made into the case you might have problem detecting the end the tape the tape drive does all tapes and the tapes all look good then either the 