14 |text from akins cbnewsd att com kay akins subject food related seizures organization summary seizures and foods lines article paulson 93apr15082558 cmb00 larc nasa gov paulson tab00 larc nasa gov sharon paulson writes posting this group hopes finding someone out there network newsland who has heard something similar what going describe here have fourteen year old daugter who experienced seizure november 1992 45am after eating kellog frosted flakes she perfectly healthy had never experienced anything like this before and there history seizures either side the family all the tests eeg mri ekg came out negative the decision was made nothing and just wait see happened again well were going along fine and the other morning april she had bowl another kellog frosted kind cereal fruit loops embarrassed admit that even bought that junk but every once while pour her bowl and think this the same kind junk she was eating when she had that seizure ten minutes later she had full blown seizures this was her first exposure sugar coated cereal since the last seizure daughter has epilepsy and attend monthly parent support group just wednesday night mother was telling how she decided throw all the junk food out and see made difference her year old seizures was having about one seizure per week she reported that she did this thursday had seizure saturday and then went weeks without seizure easter went grandma and ate candy pop anything wanted had seizure the next day she sees sensitivity nutrasweet sugar colors caffine and corn with corn she says gets very nervous and aggresive with own daughter age think she also sensitive and stays away from those foods her own she has never had gum won eat candy prefers apple cookie doesn like chocolate and won even use toothpaste her brother the other hand junk food addict hope this helps good luck
