1 |text from bcash crchh410 nosubdomain nodomain brian cash subject visit from the jehovah witnesses nntp posting host crchh410 organization bnr inc lines article 1993apr2 115300 803 batman bmd trw com jbrown batman bmd trw com writes article c4twso 8m2 ileaf com mukesh ileaf com mukesh prasad writes article 1993apr1 142854 794 batman bmd trw com jbrown batman bmd trw com writes article 1p8v1ainn9e9 matt ksu ksu edu strat matt ksu ksu edu steve davis writes bskendig netcom com brian kendig writes the earth evil because satan rules over this new one guess been while since witness bothered with are they implying that satan omniscient you might try tricking them into saying that satan all knowing and then use that statement show them how their beliefs are self contradictary satan not omniscient but does hold dominion over the earth according christian theology note not confused with theology what are the standard theologies who what created satan and why orthodox christian theology states that god created lucifer satan along with the other angels presumably because wanted beings celebrate glorify existence and life and thereby god along with him actually the whys and wherefores god motivations for creating the angels are not big issue within christian theology but god created lucifer with perfect nature and gave him along with the other angels free moral will lucifer was high angel perhaps the highest with great authority seems that his greatness caused him begin take pride himself and desire equal greater than god forgot his place created being exalted himself above god and thereby evil and sin entered creation actually the story goes that lucifer refused bow before man god commanded him lucifer was devoted god yeah there nothing genesis that says the snake was anything more than snake well talking one had legs the time too don think pointing out contradictions stories the best way show the error theology they think supernatural entity kicked the first humans out paradise because they bit into fruit that gave them special powers well they might not respond well reason and logic brian
5 |text from pmontan nswc navy mil paul montanaro subject iici q700 upgrade organization nswc lines article 1993apr15 164053 29298 thunder mcrcim mcgill edu dudek daeron mcrcim mcgill edu gregory dudek wrote article c5ha0x 11oq austin ibm com login austin ibm com writes while ago posted note asking for specs the quadra 700 and opinions the q700 upgrade iici accelerator card far responsed that noticed please let know what you think these possible upgrade paths cost efficiency pros cons etc thanks complete q700 are best obtained from your dealer some recent copy macworld macuser foggy memory suggests that the most relevant comparison factors vis vis iici are follows mhz 68040 mhz data path don recall this for sure but slower than 950 style machines for sure ethertalk card board audio out ram motherboard simm slots nubus slots more flexible build video than the uses vram comparison iici with accelerator won give you audio ethernet the same video options with 68040 accelerator cpu performance can comparable but think ends costing more greg dudek actually accelerator such the daystar mhz 68040 cheaper than upgrading q700 mhz the accelerator costs about 1400 whereas the upgrade costs 2131 just quoted from dealer however the q700 upgrade gives you very fast built video that supports monitors with bit depth and bit depth with additional vram also has scsi port capable much faster throughput than the which makes big difference you have fast hard drive the improved video and scsi features are important you you better off getting the q700 upgrade otherwise save some money and get accelerator paul
4 |text from storm mcgill marc wandschneider subject know anything about eisa nntp posting host mnementh mcgill organization socs mcgill university montreal canada lines article 1qt5nk 8o6 agate berkeley edu bing zinc cchem berkeley edu bing writes read about the development eisa some time ago but dismissed light the intense interest vesa and pci however recently was disheartened hear that isa cannot address more than 16mb ram limit that too many will hit all too soon recall that eisa will support bit transfer among other enhancements there such standard being developed very possibly but still going backwards compatible with the isa bus going the same tripe that the current eisa implementation really from what seen the pci bus will just new 32bit 33mhz intelligent bus bus controller takes care interrupts and the like not jumpers hopefully get somewhere there with the amiga zorro iii bus bus bit too much hack for liking toodlepip marc
