6 |text from martinh cac washington edu martin hunt subject announcing tcpview motif based tcp protocol analyzer organization networks and distributed computing lines keywords protocol analyzer tcp xannounce expo lcs mit edu tcpview the result several problems had have several network general sniffers which are heavily used help debug problems several hundred subnets these are good tools but they are heavy hard find when you need one limited their software expandibility difficult use upload data for analysis cannot remotely operated and cannot resolve names with dns requiring much manual manipulation the name table also sometimes use tcpdump but found too difficult for most people did not have enough information for many protocols could not used interactively could not handle tcp streams and could not read sniffer files however tcpdump did reasonable job decoding large number protocols and could easily modified tcpview attempt resolve these problems adding motif interface tcpdump and expanding its features tcpview has been tested decstation 5000 and sun under ultrix and sunos respectively should work the same systems tcpdump compiles with and gcc the dec and sun build tcpview you will need motif better the following files are available for anonymous ftp from ftp cac washington edu pub networking tcpview tar tcpview and tcpdump source code tcpview sun tar sun4 binaries tcpview dec tar dec mips ultrix binaries what tcpview adds tcpdump easier interface enhanced protocol decoding hex display frame capture based time number frames user interrupt can show ethernet addresses with manufacturer name ethernet address host table can easily follow stream highlighting out order frames can send tcp data external file filter for additional processing changes tcpdump new features now reads and writes network general sniffer files when used with the file type will automatically detected can now read and use snmp mib file the hex format has been changed new time options have been added options were added allow viewing and processing the data tcp packets bugs were fixed the relative tcp sequence numbers flag new flags read sniffer file not usually needed except for reading from stdin ttt prints delta times tttt prints times relative the first frame write sniffer save file use with print frame minus link level header hexdump format sample output 349851 jeff cac washington edu 1285 nic funet ftp win 16384 0000 0010 0020 print tcp data hexdump format used with write tcp data stdout use with eliminate timestamp write frames and tcp data stdout martin hunt martinh cac washington edu networks distributed computing university washington martin hunt martinh cac washington edu networks and distributed computing university washington
