8 |text from markm bigfoot sps mot com mark monninger subject car buying story was christ another dealer service scam nntp posting host 223 250 reply rapw20 email sps mot com organization sps distribution usa lines article 1qhs7dinnj2b col col com tvervaek col com tom vervaeke writes experience with jeep service dept while not exactly service incident had similar experience recently when bought new truck had picked out the vehicle wanted and after little haggling agreed price wrote them check for the down payment plus tax and license and told them back that evening pick the truck when returned had wait about hour before the finance guy could get when finally got there everything went smoothly until started adding the numbers then discovered that they had miscalculated the tax license about 150 then said needed another 150 from said had already agreed price and was their problem wasn giving them any more money the finance guy then brought the manager duty who proceeded give hard time reminded him that was the customer and didn think should treated like that and that didn back off could forget the whole deal made some smart remark told him where could stick snatched back check and left needless say they were not pleased the turn events early the next morning got call from the general sales manager wanting know what happened related the story and apologised profusely and asked there was anything they could change mind told him that they gave the truck for free probably still wouldn take that there were other dealers town was repeat customer theirs and that they should learn how treat customers etc etc was still pretty steamed about the whole affair gave the line about hating lose customer and they would try find solution etc etc told him not bother thanks somewhere else couple hours later the owner the dealership called all apologetic etc etc etc and said that they would cover the 150 plus knock another 400 off the price the truck told him think about and gave his private direct phone number his secretary name and assured that they valued customer etc etc etc thought about for few hours and discussed with wife and decided what the hell that was pretty decent deal called him back and accepted his offer when went back the next day pick the truck received the royal treatment everyone seemed know about the incident even the lot boy everything went smoothly and was out there new truck about mins guess reasonably satisfied customer however should not have happened the first place was bit shocked have sales person talk like that don expect them bow and grovel but sure don expect given hard time either esp when their mistake anyway happy with the truck and turned out couple hundred dollars under invoice and they paid most the first year license fee not sure whether back that dealer tho mark
