16 |text from nigel allen canrem com nigel allen subject library congress host dead sea scroll symposium april lines library congress host dead sea scroll symposium april national and assignment desks daybook editor contact john sullivan 202 707 9216 lucy suddreth 202 707 9191 both the library congress washington april symposium the dead sea scrolls will held the library congress wednesday april and thursday april the two day program cosponsored the library and baltimore hebrew university with additional support from the project judaica foundation will held the library mumford room sixth floor madison building seating limited and admission any session the symposium must requested writing see note the symposium will held one week before the public opening major exhibition scrolls from the dead sea the ancient library qumran and modern scholarship that opens the library congress april view will fragmentary scrolls and archaeological artifacts excavated qumran loan from the israel antiquities authority approximately items from library congress special collections will augment these materials the exhibition view the madison gallery through aug made possible generous gift from the project judaica foundation washington the dead sea scrolls have been the focus public and scholarly interest since 1947 when they were discovered the desert miles east jerusalem the symposium will explore the origin and meaning the scrolls and current scholarship scholars from diverse academic backgrounds and religious affiliations will offer their disparate views ensuring lively discussion the symposium schedule includes opening remarks april librarian congress james billington and norma furst president baltimore hebrew university chairing the symposium are joseph baumgarten professor rabbinic literature and institutions baltimore hebrew university and michael grunberger head hebraic section library congress geza vermes professor emeritus jewish studies oxford university will give the keynote address the current state scroll research focusing where stand today the second day the closing address will given shmaryahu talmon who will propose research agenda picking the theme how the qumran studies might proceed wednesday april other speakers will include eugene ulrich professor hebrew scriptures university notre dame and chief editor biblical scrolls from qumran the bible qumran michael stone national endowment for the humanities distinguished visiting professor religious studies university richmond the dead sea scrolls and the pseudepigrapha from special preview the exhibition will given symposium participants and guests thursday april beginning speakers will include magen broshi curator shrine the book israel museum jerusalem qumran the archaeological evidence kyle mccarter albright professor biblical and ancient near eastern studies the johns hopkins university the copper scroll lawrence schiffman professor hebrew and judaic studies new york university the dead sea scrolls and the history judaism and james vanderkam professor theology university notre dame messianism the scrolls and early christianity the thursday afternoon sessions include devorah dimant associate professor bible and ancient jewish thought university haifa qumran manuscripts library jewish community norman golb rosenberger professor jewish history and civilization oriental institute university chicago the current status the jerusalem origin the scrolls shmaryahu talmon magnas professor emeritus biblical studies hebrew university jerusalem the essential commune the renewed covenant how should qumran studies proceed will close the symposium there will ample time for question and answer periods the end each session also wednesday april the library congress and the israel antiquities authority will hold lecture esther boyd alkalay consulting conservator israel antiquities authority preserving the dead sea scrolls the mumford room 649 james madison memorial building the library congress 101 independence ave washington note for more information about admission the symposium please contact writing michael grunberger head hebraic section african and middle eastern division library congress washington 20540 canada remote systems toronto ontario 416 629 7000 629 7044
