15 |text from mailrp esa bitnet gmd subject message from space digest added forwarded space digest organization via international space university original sender isu vacation venari cmu edu distribution sci lines joint press release esa paris april 1993 esa joint training course satellite applications held italy april the united nations and the european space agency esa are jointly organising training course the applications satellite data gathered the european remote sensing satellite ers held frascati italy from april the training course will discuss the applications satellite data concerning natural resources renewable energy and the environment the training course organised for the benefit francophone african experts will hosted esrin the european space agency establishment frascati which responsible for coordination with the users data from esa remote sensing satellite twenty four experts the field remote sensing selected from francophone countries from northern western and central africa and three regional african centres will attend the two week session the course will focus remote sensing techniques and data applications particularly ers data the ers satellite developed esa and launched 1991 with the european ariane launcher carries advanced radar instrument and the first series radar remote sensing missions that will ensure availability data beyond the year 2000 the aim the training course increase the potential experts using the practical applications radar remote sensing systems natural resources renewable energy and the environment with particular emphasis applications geology and mineral prospecting oceanography and near coastal areas agriculture forestry and meteorology the education and practical training programme was developed jointly the united nations and esa the facilities and the technical support well lecturers and information documents for the training course will provided the agency lecturers the training course will include high level experts from other european and african organisations active remote sensing applications funds for the training course are being provided the united nations trust fund for new and renewable sources energy the primary contributor that fund the government italy similar training course being planned for latin american experts
