11 |text from nlu xenon stanford edu nelson subject sharks review part defensemen organization computer science department stanford university lines finally got back with great thanks mark spiegel for saving and sending rob zettler season 4th acquired from minnesota dispersal draft grade zettler gave the sharks every bit got this year unfortunately this still wasn enough make him any more than marginal nhler that works hard for sure but better than average defense and prone costly penalties and defensive lapses times while being basically offensive zero goal and assists games would hardpressed make the team next year david williams season 2nd acquired free agent from new jersey grade imo williams was the most valuable defenseman for the sharks playing combination good offense goals and assists games and good defense but playing the first part this season kansas city was good neither offensively nor defensively this year then appears that was fluke although improved towards the end the season was prone being out position defensively and did not demonstrate the playmaking skills that made him the team leading scorer among defensemen last year would also hardpressed make the team next year jayson more season 2nd acquired from montreal expansion draft grade after being touted the team top defensive prospects training camp before more had rather disappointing was not particularly good defensively and had just points games then proceeded improve his game massively this season becoming the team most reliable defenseman whom the team can count night and night out play steady defense and providing occasional but only occasional offensive flash offensively was even more disappointing than last year points games but his defense improved tremendously probably best the defensive part defense combination with offensive defenseman neil wilkinson season 4th acquired from minnesota dispersal draft grade wilkinson was probably the team top defensive defenseman however partially because injuries was not the same this year missed games total due nagging knee and back injuries and seemed slowed even when playing then had often saved his defensive partners that they are there all but also had some solid games and can complete healthy can still force sandis ozolinsh season 1st acquired 2nd round pick entry draft grade the time his injury december against the philadelphia flyers ozolinsh was well track imo the team mvp serious knee injury that game though forced him miss the rest the season games but still finished the team top scorer among defensemen points which course tells more about the lack offense the sharks had from their defensemen but also tells ozolinsh abilities the time was playing very good defense along with excellent offense was still susceptible called rookie mistakes but was probably the defenseman who made the least them the team rookie veteran can come back from his injuries ready star doug zmolek season 1st acquired from minnesota dispersal draft grade zmolek had basically solid and durable year being one the only two sharks play all games the season was solid defense but after being billed offensive defenseman didn show points was also prone penalties and his 229 penalty minutes was second the team however that was also indication that was fearly when facing tough physical opponents and was his best when playing physically but become fixture this league needs improve both offensively and defensively and cut down the number power plays gives opponents calgary flames macinnis for norris gary roberts for hart and smythe edmonton oilers for playoffs next year stay edmonton nelson claudius leland stanford edu rec sport hockey contact for the san jose sharks
