6 |text from dbl visual com david lewis subject comp windows frequently asked questions faq summary useful information about the window system reply faq craft uunet net faq maintenance address organization visual inc expires sun may 1993 gmt lines 998 archive name faq part3 last modified 1993 subject where can get patches x11r5 the release new public patches the mit consortium announced the comp windows announce newsgroup patches themselves are available via ftp from export and from other sites from which x11 available they are now also distributed through the newsgroup comp sources some source sellers may including patches their source distributions x11 people without ftp access can use the xstuff mail server now has patches for x11r5 send xstuff expo lcs mit edu the subject line send fixes where the name the patch and usually just the number the patch here are few complications fix four parts you need request and separately the file sungx which was part earlier patch was released with patch note the file doesn work with solaris fix two parts and fix three parts 13a 13b and 13c fix two parts 16a and 16b fix replaces the r5fix test1 for the test suite which previously was optional fix also needs pexlib tar which you can obtain from xstuff asking for pexlib 1234 fix parts 22a through 22i subject what the xstuff mail archive the xstuff server mail response program that means that you mail request and mails back the response any the four possible commands must the first word line the xstuff server reads your entire message before does anything you can have several different commands single message unless you ask for help the xstuff server treats the subject header line just like any other line the message the archives are organized into series directories and subdirectories each directory has index and each subdirectory has index the top level index gives you overview what the subdirectories and the index for each subdirectory tells you what the command help send help causes the server send you more detailed version this help file your message contains line whose first word index then the server will send you the top level index the contents the archive there are other words that line that match the name subdirectories then the indexes for those subdirectories are sent instead the top level index for example you can say send index fixes index fixes message that requests index cannot request data your message contains line whose first word send then the xstuff server will send you the item named the rest the line name item you give its directory and its name for example send fixes you may issue multiple send requests the xstuff server contains many safeguards ensure that not monopolized people asking for large amounts data the mailer set that will send more than fixed amount data each day the work queue contains more requests than the day quota then the unsent files will not processed until the next day whenever the mailer run send its day quota sends the requests out shortest first some mailers produce mail headers that are unusable for extracting return addresses you use such mailer you won get any response you happen know explicit path you can include line like path foo bar bitnet mitvma mit edu path bar foo frotz the body your message and the daemon will use the xstuff server itself can reached xstuff expo lcs mit edu your mailer deals notation try sending someplace mit eddie expo lcs mit edu xstuff based information from the mit consortium subject where can get x11r4 source and binaries integrated computer solutions inc ships x11r4 half inch quarter inch and tk50 formats call 617 621 0060 for ordering information the free software foundation 617 876 3296 sells x11r4 half inch tapes and qic cartridges yaser doleh doleh math kent edu box 1301 kent 44240 making x11r4 available format tapes track and sun cartridges european sites can obtain free x11r4 distribution from jamie watson who may reached chx400 pan pan non standard logi