15 |text from dnadams nyx edu dean adams subject ariane mission data organization university denver dept math comp sci lines 114 arianespace flight flight was originally intended carry the hughes 601 series galaxy satellite but the payload was withdrawn just prior flight the 56th ariane launch now scheduled place the astra and arsene satellites into improved geostationary transfer orbit gto with inclination reduced degrees and apogee altitude increased 150 this will the 28th launch ariane and the first the 42l configuration with liquid strap boosters pal will launched from the newly refurbished ariane launch complex ela kourou french guiana the launch vehicle performance requirement for this mission 147 which 944 represents the satellite mass the total vehicle mass liftoff 361 778 required orbit characteristics perigee altitude 200 apogee altitude 160 injection inclination degrees the ariane 42l lift off for flight scheduled thursday april 1993 soon possible within the following launch window kourou time gmt washington launch vehicle ariane 42l this three stage liquid fueled launcher with two liquid fueled strap boosters the first stage l220 built aerospatiale and powered liquid fueled viking engines the second stage l33 built mbb erno and powered single viking engine both the viking and engines are manufactured sep the first and second stages use biliquid uh25 n2o4 fuel the third stage h10 built aerospatiale and powered cryogenic fueled engine built sep the two strap boosters pal are each powered viking engine also built sep which use the same biliquid fuel the first and second stages the fully assembled launch vehicle stands meters high the pad uses the type ariane short payload fairing flight profile liquid strap booster jettison first stage separation second stage ignition fairing jettison second stage separation third stage ignition third stage shutdown orbit injection astra separation cyclade adapter separation arsene separation end ariane mission payloads astra the third spacecraft the fleet societe europeenne des satellites broadcast direct homes all over europe built hughes will the second 601 launched ariane total mass lift off 790 mass geo insertion 700 dry mass 180 board power 300 end life nominal lifetime years span solar panels orbit position degrees east over africa transmission capacity channels band via transponders flight operations solar array deployment about days after lift off first apogee motor firings about hours after lift off 4th apogee arsene the first spacecraft built the european space industry for the benefit the world amateur radio community total mass lift off 154 mass geo insertion dry mass board power end life nominal lifetime years spacecraft dimensions 96m orbital parameters 20000 36000 inclination period transmission capacity band transponder 446 ghz vhf uhf 145 435 mhz launch coverage all ariane missions are broadcast live via satellite from kourou coverage begins minutes before launch and continues until all payloads have been deployed this mission will likely carried the galaxy however could galaxy another satellite what the european satellite normally used for ariane coverage dean adams
