 computer professionals call for public debate new government encryption initiative computer professionals for social responsibility cpsr today called for the public disclosure technical data underlying the government newly announced public encryption management initiative the new cryptography scheme was announced today the white house and the national institute for standards and technology nist which will implement the technical specifications the plan nist spokesman acknowledged that the national security agency nsa the super secret military intelligence agency had actually developed the encryption technology around which the new initiative built according nist the technical specifications and the presidential directive establishing the plan are classified open the initiative public review and debate cpsr today filed series freedom information act foia requests with key agencies including nsa nist the national security council and the fbi for information relating the encryption plan the cpsr requests are keeping with the spirit the computer security act which congress passed 1987 order open the development non military computer security standards public scrutiny and limit nsa role the creation such standards cpsr previously has questioned the role nsa developing the called digital signature standard dss communications authentication technology that nist proposed for government wide use 1991 after cpsr sued nist foia lawsuit last year the civilian agency disclosed for the first time that nsa had fact developed that security standard nsa due file papers federal court next week justifying the classification records concerning its creation the dss david sobel cpsr legal counsel called the administration apparent commitment the privacy electronic communications reflected today official statement step the right direction but questioned the propriety nsa role the process and the apparent secrecy that has thus far shielded the development process from public scrutiny time when are moving towards the development new information infrastructure vital that standards designed protect personal privacy established openly and with full public participation not appropriate for nsa agency with long tradition secrecy and opposition effective civilian cryptography play leading role the development process cpsr national public interest alliance computer industry professionals dedicated examining the impact technology society cpsr has chapters the and maintains offices palo alto california cambridge massachusetts and washington for additional information cpsr call 415 322 3778 mail cpsr csli stanford edu regards ian ameline
