2 |text from robert cpuserver acsc com robert grant subject virtual reality for the cheap organization uscacsc los angeles lines 187 distribution world reply robert cpuserver acsc com robert grant nntp posting host cpuserver acsc com everyone thought that some people may interested software these groups announcing the release multiverse multiverse multi user non immersive windows based virtual reality system primarily focused entertainment research features client server based model using berkeley sockets limit the number users apart from performance generic clients customizable servers hierachical objects allowing attachment cameras and light sources multiple light sources ambient point and spot objects can have extension code handle unique functionality easily attached functionality client the client built around fast render loop basically changes things when told the server and then renders image from the user viewpoint also provides the server with information about the user actions which can then communicated other clients and therefore other users the client designed generic other words you don need develop new client when you want enter new world this means that resources can spent enhancing the client software rather than adapting the adaptations will explained moment occur the servers this release the client software supports the following functionality hierarchical objects with associated addressing multiple light sources and types ambient point and spot user interface panels colour polygonal rendering with phong shading optional wireframe for faster frame rates mouse and keyboard input some people may disappointed that this software doesn support the powerglove input device this not because can but because don have one this will however one the first enhancements server this where customization can take place the following basic support provided this release for potential world server developers transparent client management client message handling this may not sound like much but takes away the headache accepting and terminating clients and receiving messages from them the application writer can work with the assumption that things are happening locally things get more interesting the object extension functionality this what provided allow you animate your objects server selectable extension installation what this means that you can decide which objects have extended functionality your world basically you call the extension initialisers you want event handler registration when you develop extensions for object you basically write callback functions for the events that you want the object respond current events supported init move change collide terminate collision detection registration you want your object respond collision events just provide some basic information the collision detection management software your callback will activated when collision occurs this software kept separate from the worldserver applications because the application developer wants build library extended objects from which choose the following all you need make world server application provide initworld function this where you choose what object extensions will supported plus any initialization you want provide positionobject function this where you determine where place new client provide installworldobjects function this where you load the world wld file for new client provide getworldtype function this where you tell new client what persona they should have provide animateworld function this where you can wild minimum you should let the objects move calling move function and let the server sleep for bit avoid outrunning the clients that all there and prove here are the line counts for the three world servers provided generic lines dactyl 270 lines more complicated collision detection due the stairs will probably improved with future versions dogfight lines location this software located the following site ftp washington edu directory pub virtual worlds file multiverse tar futures client texture mapping more realistic rendering buffering similar gouraud shading hmd support etc etc server physical modelling gravity friction etc enhanced object management interaction etc etc both improved comms hope this provides people with good understanding the multiverse software unfortunately comes with practically zero documentation and not sure whether that will ever able rectified hope people enjoy this software and that useful our explorations the virtual universe certainly found fascinating developing and would love add support for the powerglove and hmd finally one major disclaimer this totally amateur code that mean there support for this code other than what out the kindness heart you out pure desperation provide cannot held responsible for anything good bad that may happen through the use this code use your own risk disclaimer over course you love would like here from you and anyone with positive contributions criticisms also encouraged contact anyone who hates dev null and anyone wants let this for living you know where write thanks robert robert acsc com
