on calls etc programming library bdf bitmap distribution format human readable format for uncompiled fonts gui graphical user interface uil the user interface language part osf motif which lets programmers specify widget hierarchy simple outline form wcl the widget creation language package which extends the understanding the resource format such that widget hierarchy and actions the widgets can specified through the resources file gil the file format put out sun openwindows developers guide uims user interface management system subject what the icccm how write friendly applications the inter client communication conventions manual one the official consortium standards documents that define the environment describes the conventions that clients must observe coexist peacefully with other clients sharing the same server you are writing clients you need read and understand the icccm particular the sections discussing the selection mechanism and the interaction between your client and the window manager get either part the distribution from mit the later editions the scheifler gettys window system book appendix the new version reilly volume protocol reference manual version old copies their volume obsolete the version the digital press book much more readable thanks the efforts digital press editors improve the english and the presentation from david rosenthal the icccm was updated for updates are published reilly programmer supplement for release the complete document the tapes alternate definition the icccm generally the rtfm and the most important the least read documents subject what the consortium and how join the mit consortium was formed january 1988 further the development the window system and has its major goal the promotion cooperation within the computer industry the creation standard software interfaces all layers the window system environment mit role provide the vendor neutral architectural and administrative leadership required make this work membership the consortium open any organization there are two categories membership member for large organizations and affiliate for smaller organizations most the consortium activities take place via electronic mail with meetings when required designs and specifications take shape interest groups are formed from experts the participating organizations typically small multi organization architecture team leads the design with others acting close observers and reviewers once complete specification produced may submitted for formal technical review the consortium proposed standard the standards process typically includes public review outside the consortium and demonstration proof concept your involvement the public review process member affiliate the consortium welcomed write bob scheifler mit consortium laboratory for computer science 545 technology square cambridge 02139 for complete information see the xconsortium man page from the x11r4 distribution from which this information adapted subject just what are open look and motif open look and motif are two graphical user interfaces guis open look was developed sun with help from and many industry reviewers motif was developed the open software foundation osf with input from many osf members open look primarily user interface specification and style guide there are several toolkits which can used produce open look applications motif includes api specification the only sanctioned motif toolkit the one from osf however there are other toolkits which can used produce programs which look and behave like osf motif one these parcplace formerly solbourne virtual toolkit which provides objects the style open look and motif the user choice open look gui also the name product from comprising their open look intrinsics toolkit and variety applications thanks ian darwin ian com subject just what openwindows open windows sun product that encompasses window system that combines news and x11 compliant server news user interface specification open look and series toolkits that implement including the sunview like xview and the based olit xlib and implementations and number utilities olwm window manager filemgr shelltool etc thanks frank greco fgreco govt shearson com subject just what decwindows decwindows dec product that encompasses x11 server the xui toolkit including the dwt widget set and uil xlib and implementations session manager and number utilities dxwm window manager dxcalendar dxpsview etc some point motif flavors the toolkit and applications will shipped subject what pex pex the phigs extension phigs stands for programmer hierarchical interactive graphics system and essentially library functions that simplifies the creation and manipulation graphics many platforms are capable performing hardware the computations involved rendering objects the extension allows the client phigs this case take advantage the specialized hardware for graphics sun microsystems currently contracted develop freely redistributable copyright similar the current copyright sample implementation source and documentation are available the release several vendors are currently selling independently developed pex servers for their workstations and terminals last modified subject what low bandwidth lbx xremote ppp slip cslip there are several options for using over serial lines slip serial line this both mechanism and protocol for sending packets over point point serial links has been around for several years and implementations are available for many the major tcp implementations most terminal vendors supply this checkoff item although nobody really ever uses since horribly slow the tcp headers add bytes per packet and the tcp encoding the protocol rather verbose rightfully optimized for packing and unpacking over high speed links cslip compressed header slip this variant slip that compresses the bytes tcp headers down about bytes still doesn anything about reencoding the protocol modems that compression can help but they increase packet latency takes time dribble the uncompressed data through typical serial interfaces plus the compression assembly time ppp point point protocol this emerging standard for point point links over serial lines that has more complete set option negotiation than slip growing number people see the combination ppp for the serial line management and cslip for the header compression becoming common for running normal tcp protocols over serial lines running raw over the wire still needs compression somewhere make usable xremote this the name both protocol and set products originally developed ncd for squeezing the protocol over serial lines addition using low level transport mechanism similar ppp cslip xremote removes redundancies the protocol sending deltas against previous packets and using lzw compress the entire data stream this work done either pseudo server proxy running the host terminal server there are several advantages doing compression outside the modem you don have have compressing modems there you wouldn otherwise using them you were going directly connected and reduces the overhead cutting down the number bytes that have cross the serial interface and addition the effects reduces the latency delivering packets not requiring the modem buffer the data waiting for blocks compress lbx low bandwidth this consortium project that working standard for this area being chaired ncd and xerox and using ncd xremote protocol stepping stone developing the new protocol lbx will beyond xremote adding proxy caching commonly used information connection setup data large window properties font metrics keymaps etc and more efficient encoding the protocol the hope have standard ready for public review the first half next year and sample implementation available additional technical information about how xremote works and few notes how lbx might different are available via anonymous ftp from export lcs mit edu contrib the following files xremote slides slides describing xremote xremote lbx diffs more slides describing some lbx information provided jim fulton jim ncd com there also set slides export from jim fulton talk the 7th mit technical conference subject topic using day day life subject what are all these different window managers the window manager just another client not part the window system although enjoys special privileges and there single window manager instead there are many which support different ways for the user interact with windows and different styles window layout decoration and keyboard and colormap focus approximate chronological order generally the more recent ones are more conformant with the icccm this simple title bar window manager was phased out uwm the universal window manager still popular for its speed although very outdated moved contrib the tape twm old tom window manager was among the first non mit window managers and offered the user great deal customization options parenting window manager awm the ardent window manager remains hotbed for hackers and offers some features dynamic menus not found more current window managers cwm cwm part the andrew system rtl siemen window manager tiles windows that they don overlap and resizes the window with the focus its preferred size dxwm digital dxwm part the decwindows offering hpwm window manager offers look precursor mwm mwm the motif window manager part the osf motif toolkit tekwm tektronix window manager offering olwm sun olwm implements the open look gui and some the style guide functionality olwm ditto gwm bull generic window manager emulates others with built lisp interpreter version the contrib tape avahi inria and export lcs mit edu m_swm the sigma window manager the tape pswm sun postscript based pswm part the openwindows release swm solbourne swm based the toolkit and offers multiple gui support and also panned virtual window configuration information comes from the resources file twm new mit new tab window manager from the tape reworked twm and the basis for several derivatives including the one the tape vtwm vtwm offers some the virtual desktop features swm with single root window implementation based the twm and available archive servers new version vtwm based and available from export tvtwm tom virtual tab window manager also based the twm and provides virtual desktop modeled the virtual root window swm available archive servers olvwm the vtwm style virtual desktop added sun olwm available archive servers version export mvwm the vtwm style virtual desktop added osf mwm beta version floating around most recently from suresh unipalm but requires source license osf motif ncdwm the window manager local ncd terminals offers mwm look xdswm the window manager local visual technology terminals ctwm claude lecommandeur lecom sic epfl modification the twm offers virtual screens the fashion vuewm source export version also offers the window overview used vtwm and tvtwm vuewm mwm based window manager offers configurable workspaces 4dwm sgi enhanced mwm piewm this version tvtwm offers pie menus subject why does session exit when kill window manager sic needn what probably happening that you are running your window manager the last job your xsession xinitrc file your session runs only long the last job running and killing your window manager equivalent logging out instead run the window manager the background and the last job instead invoke something safe like exec xterm name login iconic any special client your devising which exits some user action your session will continue until you explicitly logout this window whether not you kill restart your window manager subject can save the state session like toolplaces does although known window manager directly supports such feature which may equivalent writing out xinitrc xsession file naming the geometry and wm_command each application but olvwm may have something close there contributed application which does much what you are looking for although not complete the sunview program toolplaces look for the application xplaces archive server near you there are several versions this program floating around look for recent vintage some new pseudo session managers such vuewm provide for the saving sessions including information the geometry currently running applications and the resource database bjxrn stabell bjoerns staff uit subject how use another window manager with dec session manager dec session manager will start dxwm default override this add your xdefaults file something like this line naming the full pathname windowmanagername wherever usr bin x11 your_favorite_wm subject how change the keyboard auto repeat rate you can turn auto repeat off using xset off the protocol however doesn provide for varying the auto repeat rate which capability not supported all systems some servers running systems that support this however may provide command line flags set the rate start time you have control over server start see the man pages for xinit and xdm you can invoke the server with the chosen settings for example you can start the xsun server from mit with the options ar1 350 ar2 reduce the sensitivity the keyboard subject how remap the keys keyboard produce string there method arranging for particular string produced when you press particular key the xmodmap client which useful for moving your ctrl and esc keys useful places just rearranges keys and does not macro expansion some few clients including xterm and several based editors accept translation resource such xterm vt100 translations override key string setenv display unix which permits the shorthand pressed reset the display locally within xterm takes effect for new xterm clients include control characters the string use nnn where nnn the octal encoding the control character you want include window managers which could provide this facility not yet nor has special remapper client been made available david lewis faq craft uunet net just the faqs joe friday david lewis temporarily but not speaking for visual inc day dbl visual com evening david craft uunet net
