19 |text from clinton campaign92 org clinton gore subject clinton press release usia appointments organization project gnu free software foundation 675 mass ave cambridge 02139 usa 617 876 3296 lines 101 nntp posting host life mit edu the white house office the press secretary _________________________________________________________________ for immediate release april 1993 american university president joseph duffey named head usia mica chair board for international broadcasting washington president clinton today announced his intention nominate american university president and former state department assistant secretary joseph duffey director the united states information agency the president also designated daniel mica chairman the board for international broadcasting joe duffey expertise the fields education communications and foreign affairs vast and will serve him well takes the helm usia and works promote the ideals democracy and freedom abroad the president said president american university washington since 1991 duffey previously served nine years chancellor and president the university massachusetts amherst 1977 served assistant secretary state education and cultural affairs the state department duffey served chairman the national endowment for the humanities under both presidents carter and reagan 1978 and 1980 duffey served united states delegate the general conference the united nations educational scientific and cultural organization 1991 duffey served joint head the delegation observing national elections ethiopia usia which celebrates its 40th anniversary this year independent foreign affairs agency within the executive branch that explains and supports foreign policy and national security interests abroad through wide range information programs among the agency programs are the fulbright academic program voice america the worldnet satellite television system and network overseas libraries and cultural centers the agency has more than 210 posts more than 140 countries more press release mica becomes chairman the board for international broadcasting after serving member the board since 1991 dan mica has done excellent job the board international broadcasting and expect will continue chairman promote the cause democracy abroad the president said biographical sketches the appointees follow joseph duffey has served president american university since 1991 prior his tenure american duffey served chancellor and president the university massachusetts amherst 1982 and guest scholar the brookings institution 1982 served chairman the national endowment for the humanities from 1977 and assistant secretary state education and cultural affairs with the department state 1977 duffey holds honorary degrees from american colleges and universities 1980 was named commander the order the crown the king belgium and has been member the council foreign relations since 1979 duffey received from marshall university 1954 from the andover newton theological school 1958 stm from yale university 1963 and from the harvard seminary foundation 1969 duffey member the national business higher education forum and founder and chairman the western massachusetts economic development conference duffey married anne wexler and has four sons daniel mica former representative from the 14th district florida and has served the board international broadcasting since 1991 during his tenure congress from 1979 served the house committee foreign relations and was appointed president reagan the congressional representative the united nations
