 has been the committee senior trade counsel responsible for drafting trade legislation and reports planning and conducting hearings managing legislation the senate floor and conferences with the house overseeing variety executive branch agencies including the department commerce she was previously staff counsel for the committee dunn holds history from the university kentucky from the university kentucky college law and from the georgetown university law center christopher finn the executive vice president equities for the american stock exchange previous positions has held have included senior vice president the air and water technologies corporation chief staff senator daniel moynihan deputy commissioner the new york state department economic development and chief legislative aide congressman james jones finn graduate harvard college joan yim professional planner with over years experience community based planning policy analysis project design and management inter agency coordination and government affairs from 1975 she was with the hawaii office state planning planner issues relating natural resource and coastal zone management and public infrastructure financing among other issues currently she supervising planner with the honolulu firm parsons brinckerhogg quade douglas before going work for the state she was executive neighborhood commission secretary for the city and county honolulu and chair the kaneohe community planning committee democratic national committeewoman yim holds from connecticut college and pursued graduate studies the university hawaii more april 1993 page two alice maroni professional staff member the house armed services committee specializing defense budget issues she previously worked national defense specialist the foreign affairs and national defense division the congressional research service and international risk analyst for rockwell international she has written extensively defense budget related topics maroni received her from mount holyoke college and from the fletcher school law and diplomacy tufts university she has also completed the senior service program the national war college and harvard program for senior executives national and international security deborah castleman currently leave from rand where she space and defense policy analyst she was advisor the clinton gore campaign space science and technology and national security issues prior joining rand 1989 castleman held engineering positions with the hughes space and communications group general dynamics and electrac inc she served avionics technician the air force from 1974 castleman holds electrical and electronic engineering from california state polytechnic university electrical engineering from the california institute technology and international studies from claremont graduate school
