18 |text from arens isi edu yigal arens subject more adl spying case organization usc information sciences institute lines 222 distribution world nntp posting host grl isi edu los angeles times tuesday april 1993 new details extensive adl spy operation emerge inquiry transcripts reveal nearly years espionage man who infiltrated political groups richard paddock times staff writer san francisco the outside world roy bullock was small time art dealer who operated from his house the castro district reality was undercover spy who picked through garbage and amassed secret files for the anti defamation league for nearly years his code name the prominent jewish organization was cal and was successful infiltrating political groups that was once chosen head arab american delegation that visited rep nancy pelosi san francisco her washington office for time cal tapped into the phone message system the white aryan resistance learn hate crimes from police sources obtained privileged personal information least 394 people and met surreptitiously with agents the south african government trade his knowledge for crisp new 100 bills these are among the secrets that bullock and david gurvitz former los angeles based operative divulged extensive interviews with police and the fbi growing scandal over the nation wide intelligence network operated the anti defamation league officials the anti defamation league while denying any improper activity have said they will cooperate with the investigation they have refused discuss bullock and gurvitz transcripts the interviews among nearly 700 pages documents released san francisco prosecutors last week offer new details the private spy operation that authorities allege crossed the line into illegal territory times the intelligence activities took cloak and dagger air with laundered payments shredded documents hotel rendezvous with foreign agents and code names like ironsides and flipper one occasion gurvitz recounts received tip that pro palestinian activist was about board plane bound for haifa israel although the anti defamation league publicly denies any ties israel gurvitz phoned israeli consular official warn him shortly afterward another official called gurvitz back and debriefed him the court papers also added the mystery tom gerard former cia agent and san francisco police officer accused providing confidential material from police files the anti defamation league gerard fled the philippines last fall after was interviewed the fbi but left behind briefcase his police locker its contents included passports driver licenses and identification cards different names identification cards his own name for four american embassies central america and collection blank birth certificates army discharge papers and official stationery from various agencies also the briefcase were extensive information death squads black hood apparently for use interrogations and photos blindfolded and chained men investigators suspect that gerard and other police sources gave the adl confidential driver license vehicle registration information vast number people including many 500 members one target group the arab american anti discrimination committee each case obtaining such data from law enforcement officer would constitute felony san francisco police inspector ron roth noted affidavit for search warrant the anti defamation league self described jewish defense and civil rights organization acknowledges has long collected information groups that are anti semitic extremist racist the adl fact finding division headed irwinn suall new york enjoys reputation for thoroughness and has often shared its information with police agencies and journalists however evidence seized from bullock computer shows kept files least 950 groups all political stripes including the american civil liberties union earth island institute the united farm workers jews for jesus mother jones magazine the center for investigative reporting the gritz for president committee the asian law caucus and the aids activist group act the computer files also included information several members congress including pelosi house armed services committee chairman ron dellums berkeley and former republican rep pete mccloskey from the bay area their statements bullock and gurvitz said the anti defamation league has collected information political activists the los angeles area for more than years they said they worked closely with three los angeles county sheriff deputies who specialized intelligence work los angeles police department anti terrorism expert and san diego county sheriff department intelligence officer spokesman for the los angeles sheriff department said knew nothing any contact between the deputies and the adl the los angeles police department which earlier refused cooperate with the investigation and the san diego sheriff department declined comment bullock one the most intriguing characters the spy drama although not jewish began working undercover volunteer for the adl and the fbi indiana 1954 after reading book about man who infiltrated the communist party bullock moved los angeles 1960 and was given paid position the adl intelligence operative told authorities the mid 1970s moved san francisco and continued his spy operations and down the west coast keep his identity secret his salary has always been funneled through beverly hills attorney bruce hochman who has never missed payment more than years bullock said was investigator for the adl investigated any and all anti democratic movements bullock said officially only contract worker with bruce hochman that way the league would not officially connected with bullock said became master infiltrating groups from communists arab american gay radicals skinheads usually using his own name but once adopting the alias elmer fink one kind told police recent years however his adl affiliation has increasingly become known and one point was confronted skinhead armed with shotgun who threatened kill him the mid 1980s helped san francisco police solve bombing synagogue combing through the trash extremist cory phelps and matching handwriting with samples threatening letter obtained police part because this investigation became close friends with gerard who the time was working the san francisco police intelligence division bullock frequently searched through the garbage target groups fbi report noted how investigated one palestinian group bullock would write reports based what found the trash and would share the reports with gerard bullock also gave the trash gerard for gerard examine gerard would later return the trash bullock from wide range sources bullock compiled files 876 individuals and more than 950 political groups gerard whose files contained many identical entries kept files 011 people 1987 bullock and gerard began selling some their vast wealth information the south african government bullock tells meetings secretly with south african agents san francisco hotels and receiving envelopes filled with thousands dollars new 100 bills bullock insists the information sold consisted data culled only from public sources once rewrote innocuous item published san francisco chronicle columnist herb caen about south african bishop desmond tutu and the wife prominent attorney melvin belli and submitted his own work bullock said was gerard who sold official police intelligence bullock said split about 000 from the south african government evenly with gerard telling him one point may gay but straight arrow his interviews with the police and fbi bullock talked freely about engaging certain activities that prosecutors say would appear violate the law for example bullock admitted receiving driver license records and criminal histories from gerard about people fraction the confidential police data found his computer and said gerard gave him complete san francisco police department intelligence files various nazi groups that were supposed destroyed under department policy bullock said also received confidential fbi report the nation islam that later shredded the anti defamation league san francisco office bullock seemed proud his operation eavesdrop which used paid informant code named scumbag help tap into white aryan resistance phone message network listening the messages left members the right wing group for short time was wonderful told police los angeles adl operative gurvitz was hired about four years ago fact finder keep intelligence files and occasionally undercover the meetings target groups among other things told san francisco authorities the los angeles adl office kept record any arab american who had anti israel leanings who wrote letter newspaper expressing such sentiment gurvitz was recently forced resign after incident which attempted misuse the adl intelligence network seek revenge rival who got job gurvitz wanted the simon wiesenthal center for holocaust studies gurvitz got confidential police data the rival and threatened expose him jewish spy right wing hate group gurvitz has since begun cooperating with police and the fbi the probe providing considerable information about the adl operation unlike bullock has been assured not subject the investigation gurvitz declined through his father los angeles interviewed the times bullock attorney said his client would not comment yigal arens usc isi made arens isi edu
