14 |text from jim zisfein factory com jim zisfein subject post polio syndrome information needed please distribution world organization invention factory bbs new york city 212 274 8298v 32bis reply jim zisfein factory com jim zisfein lines from keith actrix gen keith stewart wife has become interested through acquaintance post polio syndrome this apparently not recognised new zealand and different symptons chest complaints are treated separately does anone have any information not sure that this condition recognised anywhere the sense disease with diagnostic criteria clear boundaries between and other diseases unique pathologic physiologic features etc but here goes with what many neurologists agree post polio syndrome patients have evidence motor neuron disease clinical examination emg and muscle biopsy the abnormalities are mostly chronic due old polio but there evidence ongoing deterioration clinically the patients complain declining strength and endurance with everyday motor tasks musculoskeletal pain nearly universal feature that doubtless contributes the impaired performance the examination shows muscle weakness and atrophy the emg shows evidence old denervation with reinnervation giant and long duration motor unit action potentials and evidence active denervation fibrillation potentials the biopsy also shows old denervation with reinnervation fiber type grouping and evidence active denervation small angulated fibers with dense oxidative enzyme staining but curiously little group atrophy post polio patients not have als als there clinically evident deterioration from one month the next post polio the patients are remarkably stable objective findings from one year the next course there are patients who had polio before who develop genuine als but als more common among polio survivors than among people who never had polio the cause post polio syndrome unknown there little evidence that post polio patients have active polio virus destructive immunologic response virus antigen there solid evidence that patients with post polio have anything different happening the motor unit anterior horn cells motor axons neuromuscular junctions and muscle fibers than patients with old polio who are not complaining deterioration both groups can have the same emg and biopsy findings the reason for these acute changes chronic disease old polio unknown possibly spinal motor neurons that have reinnervated huge numbers muscle fibers start shedding the load after several years there are couple clinical features that distinguish post polio syndrome patients from patients with old polio who deny deterioration the pps patients are more likely have had severe polio the pps patients are much more likely complain pain they also tend score higher depression scales neuropsychologic tests take this sure some will disagree after recovery from severe polio there can abnormal loading muscles tendons ligaments bones and joints that leads inflammatory and degenerative conditions affecting these structures the increasing pain superimposed the chronic but unchanging weakness leads progressive impairment motor performance and adl perhaps biased personal experience having never seen pps patient who was not limited some way pain not believe that pps patients have more rapid deterioration motor units than non pps patients those with old polio similar severity but without pps complaints slmr mail jim zisfein factory com jim zisfein
