14 |text from johnf ileaf com john finlayson subject exercise and migraine nntp posting host findog organization interleaf inc lines article 1993apr15 163133 25634 ntmtv janet ntmtv com janet jakstys writes the other day played tennis during lunch hour out tennis shape was very intense exercise got overheated and dehydrated afterwards noticed tingling sensation all over head then about hours later could feel migraine start continued drink water the afternoon took cafergot but didn help and the pain started although wasn intense usually and about 9pm that night the pain subsided this isn the first time that had migraine occur after exercise wondering anyone else has had the same experience and wonder what triggers the migraine this situation heat buildup dehydration not giving tennis there anything can besides get into shape and don play high noon prevent this janet sounds exactly like mine same circumstance same onset symptoms same cafergot uselessness same duration fact all the people know who have migraines none have been similar there such wide variation between people with respect what causes their headaches that generally don bother sharing what learned about mine but since ours seem alike here are observations don think heat per had more winter than summer dehydration could conceivably figure though try tanking before playing rather than after being shape doesn seem help much either identified four factors that make difference listed descending order importance heavy exercise sleep deprivation fasting skipped breakfast physical trauma head bonk heavy exercise has preceded all post adolescent migraines but don get migraines after every heavy exercise session one more the other factors must present usually since discovered this been nearly migraine free relapsing only once every two three years when get cocky been long maybe just don get them anymore and stop being careful hope this helpful john
