15 |text from baalke kelvin jpl nasa gov ron baalke subject jpl vlbi project meets with international space agencies organization jet propulsion laboratory lines 112 distribution world nntp posting host kelvin jpl nasa gov keywords vlbi jpl news software vax vms vnews from the jpl universe april 1993 vlbi project meets with international space agencies mcnevin members jpl space very long baseline interferometry vlbi project team recently concluded week long series meetings with officials from russia and japan the meetings were part space vlbi week held jpl early march and were intended maintain cooperation between international space agencies participating the development the space vlbi project recently approved jpl flight project set for launch 1995 space vlbi will utilize two earth orbiting spacecraft the japanese vsop vlbi space observing program satellite with its meter radio telescope and russian radioastron meter satellite both spacecraft will team with ground based radio telescopes located around the world create radio telescope network that astronomers hope will expand radio telescope observing power factor japan vsop satellite will use limited six hour orbit conduct imaging science while the russian radioastron spacecraft will exploit larger hour earth orbit conduct exploratory radio astronomy each satellite will point source target for roughly hours while approximately ground based radio telescopes will simultaneously point the same source object while within view earth according joel smith jpl project manager for the space vlbi meetings like those held jpl will permit japan and russia who have little previous experience radio interferometry establish working relationships with the radio astronomy communities that will vital during the complex observations required the space vlbi project one our main activities developing the methodology for international coordination because the two spacecraft simultaneously rely the corresponding tracking stations while 