9 |text from ryan_cousineau compdyn questor org ryan cousineau subject spagthorpe viking reply ryan_cousineau compdyn questor org ryan cousineau distribution world organization computer dynamics vancouver 604 986 9937 604 255 9937 lines 103 from viking iastate edu dan sorenson ryan_cousineau compdyn questor org ryan cousineau writes riding the hill leading house encountered liver and white springer spaniel relation the springer softail the springer spagthorpe close relation the spagthorpe viking must have missed the article the spagthorpe viking was that the one with the little illuminated dragon head the front fender style later copied indian and the round side covers not all the viking was trick little unit made way back when forties fifties when spag was trying make racing the first iteration the springer was boxer twin very similar max friz famous design but with overhead point cam see below for more the valvetrain the problem was that the thing had ground clearance whatsoever the solution was curve the cylinder bores that the ground clearance was substantially increased springer motor front viking motor front this roughly the idea except that the bores were gradually curved around radius the pistons were loath make sharp angled turn the middle their stroke the engine also had curved connecting rods accomodate the stroke the engine stuck out far because its revolutionary and still unique overhead cam system through the use clever valve timing and and extrordinarily trick valve linkage only single cam lobe was required drive both overhead valves just revolutionary was the hydraulic valve actuation which used pressurized stream oil power the waterwheel which kept the lobe spinning over one side effect that required some rather brutal engineering fixes was that until the engine oil pressure came normal the engine valve timing would more less random resulting some impressive start valve damage the solution was little hand crank that pressurized the cases before you started the beast remarkably similar the system used new porsches pressurize the oil system before the car started the cage however uses electric oil pump wimps despite this fix the engine had nasty propensity for explosively firing its valves into the pistons when cylinder would temporarily lose bit oil pressure corner the solution was run even higher oil pressures and change the gaskets and seals regularly this was feasible because was racing engine with just single overhead lobe and pushrod shaft chain towers because the hydraulic system the head the engine came almost perfect point lobe complex linkage not shown due valvestems complexity piston note that the tip was not truly vertical was about degree angle the ground and this drawing doesn show the curvature because there was none the head itself the bore curve would start about where the cylinder bore disappears this diagram the effect the pointy heads top pair gently pundits the day even said sensuously curved cylinders was much like pair finned viking horns poking out from beneath the gas tank thus the name the vik was moderately successful racer lightning fast when worked but plagued problems relating its revolutionary technology eventually was dumped when spag finally realized that racing was not where the spagthorpe name would made the machines were raced for another year two privateers and their fate approximately six vikings were made plus one possibly two springers confusing the issue one old spag staffer who swears and down that this machine was tooled for production and that many twenty thirty machines may have come off the line however modern record production viking has survived and most motorcycle historians discount this story ryan cousinetc 1982 yamaha vision xz550 black pig inverness live ride kotrb 1958 ajs 500 king rat work dod 0863 squid could afford the bike flame ryan cousineau compdyn questor org vancouver canada live slmr you aren sliding you aren riding computer dynamics bbs 604 255 993