12 |text from clipper csrc ncsl nist gov clipper chip announcement subject white house public encryption management fact sheet organization national institute standards technology distribution lines note the following was released the white house today conjunction with the announcement the clipper chip encryption technology fact sheet public encryption management the president has approved directive public encryption management the directive provides for the following advanced telecommunications and commercially available encryption are part wave new computer and communications technology encryption products scramble information protect the privacy communications and data preventing unauthorized access advanced telecommunications systems use digital technology rapidly and precisely handle high volume communications these advanced telecommunications systems are integral the infrastructure needed ensure economic competitiveness the information age despite its benefits new communications technology can also frustrate lawful government electronic surveillance sophisticated encryption can have this effect the united states when exported abroad can used thwart foreign intelligence activities critical our national interests the past has been possible preserve government capability conduct electronic surveillance furtherance legitimate law enforcement and national security interests while the same time protecting the privacy and civil liberties all citizens encryption technology improves doing will require new innovative approaches the area communications encryption the government has developed microcircuit that not only provides privacy through encryption that substantially more robust than the current government standard but also permits escrowing the keys needed unlock the encryption the system for the escrowing keys will allow the government gain access encrypted information only with appropriate legal authorization assist law enforcement and other government agencies collect and decrypt under legal authority electronically transmitted information hereby direct the following action taken installation government developed microcircuits the attorney general the united states her representative shall request manufacturers communications hardware which incorporates encryption install the government developed key escrow microcircuits their products the fact law enforcement access the escrowed keys will not concealed from the american public all appropriate steps shall taken ensure that any existing future versions the key escrow microcircuit are made widely available communications hardware manufacturers consistent with the need ensure the security the key escrow system making this decision not intend prevent the private sector from developing the government from approving other microcircuits algorithms that are equally effective assuring both privacy and secure key escrow system key escrow the attorney general shall make all arrangements with appropriate entities hold the keys for the key escrow microcircuits installed communications equipment each case the key holder must agree strict security procedures prevent unauthorized release the keys the keys shall released only government agencies that have established their authority acquire the content those communications that have been encrypted devices containing the microcircuits the attorney general shall review for legal sufficiency the procedures which agency establishes its authority acquire the content such communications procurement and use encryption devices the secretary commerce consultation with other appropriate agencies shall initiate process write standards facilitate the procurement and use encryption devices fitted with key escrow microcircuits federal communications systems that process sensitive but unclassified information expect this process proceed schedule that will permit promulgation final standard within six months this directive the attorney general will procure and utilize encryption devices the extent needed preserve the government ability conduct lawful electronic surveillance and fulfill the need for secure law enforcement communications further the attorney general shall utilize funds from the department justice asset forfeiture super surplus fund effect this purchase
