he mri reports both say have several bulging degeneratig disks and from the xrays and mri think apparent that have arthritis the reading the scan was that there are two herniations and but others hav looked the films and concluded that there are herniations the second emg and nerve conduction studies shows significant denervation compared the first emg yeah had some other horrible test called something like somatic evoked response which showed that the internal nerves are working fine anyway the bottom line that sometimes have severe pain both legs and back pain the back pain there all the time but can live with when the leg pain there need some analgesic anti inflammatory medication reduce the pain level where can work took naprosyn regulary for months every time tried stop the leg pain got worse always resume since last november have taken much less frequently and primarily for the pelvic pain have been going physical therapy for the last months times week after the first month therapist put pelvic traction she had tried earlier but had caused lot pain back this time she tried lower weight after month two the pain legs began going away but the traction aways caused discomfort lower back which could reduced with ultrasound and massage now don have nearly much pain legs fact therapist took off traction about weeks ago getting back original reason for this post even can avoid taking analgesic for headaches really can avoid them entirely because have other pain sources that force use them forgot mention that has been suggested that have back surgery but avoiding that too find the migraines difficult deal with occassionally have take off work but usually can work but reduced capacity systems engineer and lot reading and writing when the pelvic pain bad can concentrate much usually end jumping out chair every few minutes because the pain bothersome when the pain back bad can cause severe burning both legs shooting pains legs electric shock type pain feet and toes and basically when gets bad can really sit all then end spending most time home and bed even the analgesics contribute the migraines the migraines are more tolerable than the other pain sources get lot migraines average month which last days taken cafergot the first time the caffiene really got reduced the dosage but don like the side effects take more than two get diahrea get very bad headache will eventually take the cafergot neurologist wasn very helpful when told him problems with cafergot said that when sumatriptan becomes available should try that tried several other medications fiornal midrin fiornal with codeine tegretol and inderal but they either didn work couldn tolerate them what can doctor seem satisfied with just trying tolerate the pain which agree with most the time but not when have lot pain had some bad experiences with surgery heart stopped once from the anesthesia was told that was likely the succinylcholine and already had surgery several times anyway the point what saying that even analgesics can contribute migraines some people need take them tolerate other pain janice rathmann
