king you for login name godiva nectar cmu edu lvc instead lvc your initials will appear answer this prompt with ftp next you get this prompt asking your for your mail address guest login send mail address password would enter cipriani att com you enter your own mail address you get these lines similar output remote system unix using binary mode transfer files next the command prompt printed ftp you not get the line using binary mode transfer files run the command type binary now you logged the archive machine there are many directories this machine but the two you are concerned with are usr0 anon pub firearms politics rkba and usr0 anon pub firearms politics incoming there are subdirectories the rkba directory those are discussed below when you login the system your directory usr0 anon retreive files change your current directory the rkba directory with the command usr0 anon pub firearms politics rkba pub firearms politics rkba submit files change your directory the incoming directory with the command usr0 anon pub firearms politics incoming pub firearms politics incoming once you this you get another ftp prompt asking you enter another command find the names the existing files the directory you are run the command this will produce something like total 6021 karl 6932 jun 1992 dmn_gratia_ccp karl 69149 apr index karl 18965 jun 1992 knox_aw_lies karl 10930 apr 1992 s361 karl 8958 jun 1992 wsj_crimestrike karl 2649 jan academia bias karl 935 mar academics karl 36079 aug 1992 aclu and each line corresponds one file reading right left the fields are the file name the last modification date the file the size the file bytes and some permission fields which you not need concerned with get file run the command get followed the name the file you want for example get index get noduty after the file transfered your machine message like this transfer complete 19580 bytes received seconds kbytes you can repeat the get command for every file you want retreive you can use the mget