15 |text from baalke kelvin jpl nasa gov ron baalke subject successful balloon flight measures ozone layer organization jet propulsion laboratory lines distribution world nntp posting host kelvin jpl nasa gov keywords jpl news software vax vms vnews forwarded from public information office jet propulsion laboratory california institute technology national aeronautics and space administration pasadena calif 91109 818 354 5011 contact mary hardin for immediate release april 1993 1506 scientists nasa jet propulsion laboratory report the successful flight balloon carrying instruments designed measure and study chemicals the earth ozone layer the april flight from california barstow daggett airport reached altitude kilometers 121 000 feet and took measurements part program established correlate data with the upper atmosphere research satellite uars the data from the balloon flight will also compared readings from the atmospheric trace molecular spectroscopy atmos experiment which currently flying onboard the shuttle discovery launch these balloons several times year part ongoing ozone research program fact jpl actively involved the study ozone and the atmosphere three important ways said jim margitan principal investigator the balloon research campaign there are two jpl instruments the uars satellite continued the atmos experiment conducted jpl scientists and the jpl balloon research provides collaborative ground truth for those activities well data that useful its own right the measurements taken the balloon payload will add more pieces the complex puzzle the atmosphere specifically the mid latitude stratosphere during winter and spring understanding the chemistry occurring this region helps scientists construct more accurate computer models which are instrumental predicting future ozone conditions the scientific balloon payload consisted three jpl instruments ultraviolet ozone photometer which measures ozone the balloon ascends and descends through the atmosphere submillimeterwave limb sounder which looks microwave radiation emitted molecules the atmosphere and fourier transform infrared interferometer which monitors how the atmosphere absorbs sunlight launch occurred about noontime and following three hour ascent the balloon floated eastward approximately 130 kilometers per hour knots data was radioed ground stations and recorded onboard the flight ended pacific time eastern new mexico when the payload was commanded separate from the balloon needed fly through sunset make the infrared measurements margitan explained and also needed fly darkness watch how quickly some the molecules disappear will several weeks before scientists will have the completed results their experiments they will then forward their data the uars central data facility the goddard space flight center greenbelt maryland for use the uars scientists the balloon was launched the national scientific balloon facility normally based palestine tex operating under contract from nasa wallops flight facility the balloon was launched california because the west east wind direction and the desire keep the operation the southwest the balloons are made micron mil less than one thousandth inch thick plastic and are 790 000 cubic meters million cubic feet volume when fully inflated with helium 120 meters 400 feet diameter the balloons weigh between 300 and 800 kilograms 000 and 000 pounds the scientific payload weighs about 300 kilograms 000 pounds and meters six feet square meters feet high the jpl balloon research sponsored nasa upper atmosphere research program and the uars correlative measurements program ___ _____ ___ ____ ron baalke baalke kelvin jpl nasa gov jet propulsion lab ___ 525 3684 telos being cynical never helps ___ ___ pasadena 91109 correct the situation _____ _____ and causes more aggravation instead
