3 |text from rjn teal csn org robert niland subject procomm plus for windows problems nntp posting host teal csn org organization colorado supernet inc newsreader tin pl4 lines 292 kentiler matt ksu ksu edu kent iler writes have normal procomm plus for dos but been considering buying the windows version got really great reviews computer shopper have friend who connects the mainframe and unix machines here using but the screen seems have problem keeping with the modem has 400 modem 486 mhz machine can see having trouble keeping his pcplus for dos works great what after the high speed modem arrives edition apr this article applies only windows and and not dos apps not running under windows one the unadvertised limitations most current windows pcs that their 232c serial com performance seriously deficient almost everyone who purchases high speed modem 32bis pep hst discovers the problem the first time they try download file accept incoming fax 9600 after upgrading the modem overrun and retry errors abound even when the only active application the datacomm fax program the transfer completes all may take even longer than with the old 2400bps modem there are three reasons for the problem the universal asynchronous receiver transmitters uarts used most pcs are primitive ns8250 devices with single byte fifo buffers the operating system driver cannot read and flush each character high interrupt rates the next incoming character overwrites the fifo and the previous one lost dos being fairly single minded environment during datacomm can usually keep windows can windows has more operating system overhead than plain dos and interrupts often take longer service overruns are much more likely than under dos soon you report your modem vendor that you are losing data you may advised that you need upgrade 16550 more likely since there seems conspiracy ignorance about this issue you get useful advice all most the store front and mail order sources spoke with attempting solve own problem had never heard the term 16550 and many didn even know what uart was even your has ns16550a uarts and you can upgrade your mother com board add new com board you may still experience errors and overruns because the standard microsoft windows com drivers don take full advantage the 16550 windows improved this regard over but still recommend driver upgrade applications like procomm win which what use cannot get around this problem themselves you have modem card you may not have problem the modem part the card can designed aware the state the uart and avoid overrunning however wouldn want bet that the card designers were that clever and will insist 16550 uart ever buy modem card some modem cards don even have conventional uarts but they are work with standard windows drivers they need simulate one use msd exe below see what the modem card pretending the hardware situation the uarts most com ports are based national semiconductor ns8250 ns16450 chips megacells inside vlsi chips where you can replace them you can the uart type your system running the microsoft diagnostic program windows msd exe sure run dos before bringing windows the windows serial api may prevent msd from accurately identifying 16550 you run from windows dos prompt the ns16550 uart has separate byte transmit and receive fifos with configurable trigger levels and can run reliably clock rates 460 800 bps although with current modem technology there point pushing your luck going over 115 200 bps the 16550 has shorted access cycle times than the 16450 8250 the 16550 also has dma capability but not clear that any drivers ever use this for more technical info see national semiconductor application note 491 what uart component you have try locate the uart your mother board multi function card com board isa mca modem card you can find socketed component with the numbers 8250 16450 your com ports are probably buried vlsi and you won able perform chip replacement you can disable your vlsi com ports chose you can least add aftermarket com board you have one more socketed 8250 16450 chips you can buy plug ns16550afn pc16c550cn low power cmos version ics from several suppliers typically for each the chip the normal pin dual line package other styles are available but avoid any ns16550 chips without the the 16c550c are presumably all early chips have bugs although national will reportedly exchange those their own manufacture for free clone chips are available from various makers other than national the manual for the turbocom drivers states support for the following apparently equivalent chips national semiconductor 16550a 16551 16552 chips technology 82c607 texas instruments t16c550a silicon systems 73m550 vlsi 16c550 turbocom warns about the pre ns16550 and western digital 16c550 says that problems have been reported with early ibm 55sx and systems ibm reportedly will upgrade them you don have socketed 8250 16450 chips you need buy after market com multi function board this modem card situation you may hosed add new com multi function card you need either disable the com1 port you are replacing assign them com3 although watch out for irq conflicts without turbocom although cheaper cards are available the interest getting the problem solved quickly elected buy the modular circuit technology mct aio card from jdr microdevices 2233 samaritan drive san jose 95124 800 538 5000 voice 408 559 1200 voice other 800 538 5005 fax the mct aio and the important sells for bit isa card providing port type connector address and irq comments com db9m com irq ns16550afn socket com ribbon com irq ns16550afn socket parallel db25f lpt1 irq game ribbon the kit includes ribbon cable and db25f connector for the secondary com port ribbon cable connector for the game port two bulkhead plates for the ribbon based connectors and 25f adaptor cable each port can individually disabled and the com ports have rts cts dtr dcd and dsr jumpers jdr also sells super card that also has ide have heard from several people about less expensive cards with 16550s tsd systems 407 331 9130 for the card plus per 16550 greenfield trading and distributors 518 271 2473 voice 518 271 7811 fax their card one 16550 and they sell 16550afns for data systems inc 820 east highway 434 longwood 32750 phone 407 331 1424 fax 407 331 8606 2com lpt game card 16550s for have personal experience with any the firms except jdr meanwhile back the mct card from jdr only needed two serial ports and running out irqs disabled built vlsi based 8250 ports however with the turbocom driver below could have set the internals com3 and using irq sharing the software situation simply upgrading 16550 uarts will not completely solve common overrun problems the standard serial drivers don take full advantage the 16550 the windows drivers are even less capable and the windows drivers have the following limitations they enable only the receive fifo and only rates above 2400 bps they never enable the transmit fifo which results interrupt rate 10x during uploads they set the trigger level bytes too high easy for more bytes arrive before the driver can read the fifo the ports menu the control panel only allows speeds 19200 with 32bis modem sparse data and text can easily compress more suggesting that host dte connect rate 600 bps would effective the api won accept rates above cbr_128000 the api won let dos programs know there 16550 there and even did dos programs that aren 16550 aware get little benefit from 16550 port with the standard drivers they don allow irq sharing for com3 the bios doesn initialize com3 properly many systems windows provides workaround for apps that don provide port speed options above 19200 bps these problems are reportedly not solved windows dos and may may not addressed any windows releases after but before rumors suggest they may solved windows you can get replacement drivers that solve all those problems buying copy turbocom current version from bio engineering research pacific commware division 180 beacon hill lane ashland 97520 9701 503 482 2744 voice 503 482 2627 fax 503 482 2633 bbs mcimail 344 5374 compuserve 71521 760 price was around recall bio eng not set accept credit cards had send check egghead and 800 software list turbocom but far know they don stock bio not software company per they apparently needed reliable speed serial connections for house instrument application wrote their own driver discovered market for revised general purpose com driver suite they recently upgraded for windows run time licensed now have host dte connect rate set 600 bps most datacomm apps and having zero problems with downloads routinely see transfer rates that exceed 000 bps also using 115 200 bps when linking hp95lx with lossless directional uploads various remote systems are another matter because many hosts are still using antique uarts and drivers note that 19200 still the highest rate that the windows port menu control panel will allow configuring com port turbocom gets around this allowing you specify each port factor that will set the real uart rate multiple the rate passed through the windows apis and dialog boxes also have cts rts hardware flow control enabled and suggest that you the same even you only ever transfer bit ascii data xon xoff not sufficiently reliable method flow control the informal dec standard for xon xoff hysteresis that the sender may transmit another yes sixteen bytes after receipt the xoff from the receiving system device the byte fifo the 16550 clearly not big enough let rely exclusively xon xoff well respected datacomm engineer has informed that the 16550 can really cts rts all itself the dos windows environment using data rates above 115 200 may still risky even with hardware flow control 16550 with turbocom can still experience overruns very busy systems with lots apps running and serious swapping progress this your situation you may need buy processed com board but this will cost you more than 16550 turbocom upgrade review two 