15 |text from baalke kelvin jpl nasa gov ron baalke subject sirtf mission still alive organization jet propulsion laboratory lines 114 distribution world nntp posting host kelvin jpl nasa gov keywords sirtf jpl news software vax vms vnews from the jpl universe april 1993 sirtf still very much business mark whalen these times extra tight nasa budgets the very survival number missions has been uncertain but thanks major design refinements implemented recent months jpl space infrared telescope facility sirtf major project considered trouble couple years ago alive and well according project scientist michael werner lighter spacecraft revised orbit and shorter mission have added less expensive project with tremendous scientific power and bright future said werner designed follow the highly successful infrared astronomical satellite iras and cosmic background explorer cobe missions sirtf cryogenically cooled observatory for infrared astronomy from space scheduled for launch 2000 2001 plans proceed scheduled iras pioneering work space based infrared astronomy years ago allowed astronomers view the milky way never before and revealed among other things 000 galaxies and comets provided sky survey 000 times more sensitive than any previously available from ground based observations cobe has measured the infrared and microwave background radiation large angular scales and revealed new facts about the early universe but illuminate sirtf potential jim evans jpl manager astrophysics and fundamental physics pre projects recently said that the project 000 million times more capable than iras based technological advances infrared detector arrays however despite the enormous strides infrared exploration sirtf promised and the fact that was cited the highest priority new initiative for all astronomy the 1990s the national academy sciences took diet die directive from nasa headquarters last year keep the project going according werner the project now known atlas sirtf based the key factor its new design the satellite will orbit the sun instead the earth permitting the use atlas rocket launch instead the formerly proposed and heavier titan the main advantage the solar orbit that you can use all your launch capability for boosting the payload you don have carry second rocket circularize the orbit werner said the other advantage solar orbit said that better thermal environment away from the heat the earth additional major changes sirtf redesign include shortening the mission from five three years and building spacecraft that less than half heavy the original plan atlas sirtf will weigh 470 kilograms 400 pounds compared titan sirtf 500 kilograms 100 pounds all that adds less stressful launch environment werner said and cost savings more than 200 million for the launch addition increased savings the design the smaller less massive spacecraft werner said sirtf redesign came result congress telling nasa you trying too many things you want support sirtf which good project develop plan see how fits into nasa overall strategy shortly thereafter sirtf was named nasa highest priority flagship scientific mission the interdisciplinary space sciences advisory committee addition the blessing from the national academy sciences while the spacecraft and its instruments required descoping keep the project alive sirtf major scientific contribution always promised come about from its advanced infrared detector arrays which will allow images developed tens thousands times faster than before according evans until couple years ago werner said all infrared astronomy was done with single detectors very small arrays individually assembled detectors since then the department defense has developed program produce arrays tens hundreds thousands detectors rather than just few and those are very well suited for use sirtf werner noted that addition dealing with budget pressures congress currently watching nasa projects with eye out for any technological spinoff that question think have some things say said because the detectors using are straight off various military developments also sirtf will built the aerospace industry and real technological and engineering challenge addition being tremendous scientific project sirtf will used the entire astronomical community werner added but the revised three year mission puts premium observing time have educate the user community and develop program that involves early surveys and quick turnaround the data werner said the downsizing the project required reduction scope and complexity sirtf three instruments the infrared spectrograph infrared array camera and multiband imaging photometer however these reductions will only result losses efficiency rather than capability said the project hopes start phase activity 1995 which will provide detailed concept for development and design building the hardware would begin about two years later projected cost estimates evans said are 850 million 950 million very optimistic about sirtf said will provide tremendous return for the investment werner added that additional benefit from the project will the enrichment our intellectual and cultural environment people the street are very interested astronomy black holes the possibility life other planets the origin the universe and those are the kind questions sirtf will help answer ___ _____ ___ ____ ron baalke baalke kelvin jpl nasa gov jet propulsion lab ___ 525 3684 telos the aweto from new zealand ___ ___ pasadena 91109 part caterpillar and _____ _____ part vegetable
