4 |text from darrylo srgenprp com darryl okahata subject problem with adaptec 1542b scsi and jumbo tape drive reply darrylo com organization hewlett packard center for primal scream therapy newsreader tin version pl9 lines 560 ron mastus ronaldm extro ucc wrote just replaced existing dtc scsi controller with adaptec 1542b and now having trouble restoring from jumbo 250 tape drive here document that wrote some time back slightly out date now that dos has been released but much still useful darryl okahata internet darrylo com disclaimer this message the author personal opinion and does not constitute the support opinion policy hewlett packard the little green men that have been following him all day adaptec txt 1993 darrylo rel darrylo hints and tips for the adaptec 1540 1542 scsi adapter this document contains hints and tips for getting the adaptec 1540 1542 scsi adapter work with various hardware and software packages they are based upon experiences with adaptec 1542a controller and will hopefully help others however note that cannot guarantee that the following will really help you works for and the information this document could possibly cause you lose some all your files your hard disk important back the entire contents your hard disk before trying anything based upon information this document copyright 1993 darryl okahata this document may freely copied for personal use only and may not reprinted for profit publication without the consent the author please note that have connection with adaptec other than customer topics covered this document windows enhanced mode floppy controller based tape backup devices sound cards miscellaneous info please note that parts this document contain technical and sometimes terse descriptions problems for reference adaptec technical support 800 959 7274 adaptec bbs 2400 9600 408 945 7727 please send comments corrections etc via email compuserve 75206 3074 internet darrylo com windows enhanced mode the windows install program should automatically configure dos and windows for use with the adaptec 1542 however just case something went wrong going describe some the changes needed get windows working with the 1542 also you may have noticed that installing windows makes your run much slower even when you not running windows methods speeding are discussed the section called windows runs slowly msdos configuration the windows install program adds the smartdrive disk cache your config sys and autoexec bat files you follow the instructions you notice that you need use double buffering with smartdrive this the default setup you also notice that your system runs much much slower both windows and msdos see the section called windows runs slowly for some ways speeding your system windows configuration get the adaptec 1542 work with windows make sure that the 388enh section the system ini file contains the entry virtualhdirq off believe that the windows install program automatically adds this entry system ini but not sure this doesn work for you you might want try adding some more lines virtualhdirq off systemrombreakpoint false emmexclude a000 cfff you probably don need the above lines though the systemrombreakpoint entry used enable support for memory managers like qemm 386max only needed you use such programs windows runs slowly once you get windows running with the 1542 chances are that your system running much slower than before not probably because you happen using aspi4dos sys version your config sys file congratulations this appears winning solution you are very lucky whether your luck will hold out remains seen your system running much slower than before this almost definitely caused smartdrive with double buffering according the windows documentation and the microsoft technical note q81808 smartdrive double buffering required with aspi4dos sys you must use smartdrive with double buffering enabled while this works really slows down your once estimated that this slowed down factor five consider this unacceptable looked for other solutions unfortunately you cannot just disable double buffering you windows enhanced mode will not work and you might even destroy the contents your hard disk trying run windows what you can one the following use other drivers that provide double buffering opinion that the unbelievable slowness smartdrive caused either horribly inefficient double buffering bug smartdrive use driver that provides vds services vds stands for virtual dma services this standard which supported windows that allows bus mastering disk controllers like the 1542 work with windows after trashing hard disk countless times found the following solutions none which require using smartdrive note however that now getting occasional parity errors which are probably not caused these solutions but might see below while the following does not require smartdrive using some kind disk cache utility strongly recommended this makes windows run much much faster you not have the aspi4dos sys driver you not need aspi functions for controlling cdrom tape drive more than two physical hard disks etc you can add the scsiha sys driver your config sys file driver scsiha sys v386 windows needs the v386 option this driver must loaded into low memory cannot loaded into high memory and occupies about 20k november 1992 the scsiha sys driver could obtained from the adaptec bbs 408 945 7727 hopefully still there you need aspi functions and have the aspi4dos sys driver version you can use both the aspi4dos sys and scsiha sys drivers your config sys file driver aspi4dos sys driver scsiha sys v386 amazingly enough the scsiha sys driver can also loaded high assuming you have dos would have thought that this would crash system but doesn asked adaptec technical support about this and they said that loading scsiha sys high should fine long aspi4dos sys loaded low system not using scsiha sys with aspi4dos would occasionally cause windows crash upon restarting exiting windows with the additional result corrupted disk some windows grp files would corrupted for these crashes usually occurred while making different program from progman exe the default windows shell and vice versa this the reason scsiha sys may necessary have absolutely idea scsiha sys necessary with versions aspi4dos earlier than note that many people can use aspi4dos without scsiha sys they not seem have any problems all consider these people lucky others like have had all sorts problems opinion the best but not necessarily the easiest solution upgrade aspi4dos the scsiha sys driver longer needed unfortunately while you could get previous aspi4dos upgrades from the adaptec bbs the aspi4dos driver not available from the adaptec bbs far know there are only three ways get copy you can buy the new november 1992 adaptec scsi driver kit which supposedly includes aspi4dos well other drivers such cdrom drivers believe the list price around you already have copy older version aspi4dos you can supposedly contact adaptec upgrade scsi for around copy aspi4dos included central point tools for msdos note that the documentation and driver are stored different directories note further that only aspi4dos included the cdrom drivers and drivers support more than two hard disks are not included this where obtained copy aspi4dos note however that now getting occasional parity errors with windows all probability defective hardware causing this upgraded motherboard just after found the above solutions however because these parity errors occur only during disk accesses there very small but definite possibility that the parity errors are driver related for example changing the bus off timing for certain disk transfers might cause this run various memory tests for hours time and these tests have found problems this problem probably caused memory with marginal timing requirements which cause parity errors during disk transfers this why the memory tests didn find any problems the problems show only under disk however mentioning this just case isn hardware problem floppy controller based tape backup devices there are two possible problems with using the adaptec 1542 with floppy controller based tape backup device such the colorado memory systems jumbo 250 tape backups restores can take very long time the tape drive constantly starts stops starts stops etc tape operations may erratic encounter too many tape errors this problem might caused defective hardware 1542 however heard other people having similar problems and mentioning this just case not hardware problem 1542 tape backups restores take long time you have floppy controller based tape backup device you may have adjust the adaptec 1540 1542 bus off timing for best results when using the tape drive normally while doing tape backup restore the tape drive motor should continuously running with only occasional pause however the default bus timing the adaptec 1540 1542 may cause the tape drive motor start and stop start and stop every few seconds this causes needless wear the tape and tape drive however note that dirty tape head defective tape drive can also cause this make sure your tape heads are clean this also causes the tape backup restore take much much longer than necessary the problem here that these tape backups use the floppy dma transfer data memory from the tape drive and the adaptec uses dma transfer data memory from the hard disk the floppy dma needs feed data the tape drive certain rate the tape drive not fed data quickly enough the floppy dma the tape drive stops rewinds bit and restarts once enough data eventually fed the default bus timing the adaptec which really dma timing too large for example when backup done data has transferred from hard disk memory and then from memory the tape because the default timing the adaptec hogs the memory too much too much time spent transferring data from hard disk memory not enough time spent transferring data from memory the tape drive result the tape drive constantly starts and stops because data not fed quickly enough the solution change the adaptec bus off timing the default factory setting microseconds and microseconds off the bus timing needs lowered microseconds this can done one two ways you have aspi4dos you can use the option for example use bus timing microseconds which means that use the following line config sys file device aspi4dos sys note that there space between the and the you don have aspi4dos your only recourse try find program called setscsi exe which very difficult find the reason that adaptec for reasons their own does not seem want this widely distributed once asked someone who worked for adaptec and they asked not upload anywhere you have anonymous ftp access the internet you could try using archie hunt down copy believe that there are couple sites that have you find copy you run like setscsi this adjusts the bus timing microseconds running setscsi exe without any arguments resets the bus timing back the factory defaults note that seems that you cannot use setscsi exe you use aspi4dos setscsi exe crashed system aspi4dos was loaded could use setscsi exe with scsiha sys however not lower the bus timing below microseconds increase above microseconds you lower too low the hard disk throughput will suddenly drop your system will feel slower for microseconds works fine this value may work fine for you you may have adjust downwards little once you lowered the bus timing tape backups and restores should run faster also not experiment with the bus off times with the other options that have intentionally not described unless you know what you are doing bad combinations can cause parity errors and worse starving memory refresh program called bustifix exe exists the adaptec bbs unless this has been upgraded since last checked which has been while this self extracting archive containing batch file and couple other files this batch file was supposed allow one set the bus off times for the 1540 1542 and others however when tried running this program with 1542a system crashed the time was running scsiha sys and didn check see there was conflict with maybe this old program works only with the 1542b although the docs say that works with the 1542a erratic tape operations too many tape errors this problem may may not exist although existed system hardware problem just particular 1542 could cause however heard other people having similar problems and mentioning this just case isn hardware problem just 1542 symptoms this problem which persists even after cleaning the tape head backing tape encounters unusable sector detected errors resulting aborted tape backup tape backup works but the tape compare fails the tape drive starts stops starts stops etc much too often unlike the above mentioned problem tape backups restores take long time where the tape drive starts and stops every few seconds this kind starting stopping occurs every few seconds fastback plus does not find see any tape backup devices other programs like central point backup and the cms jumbo software assuming that you have cms jumbo 250 tape drive can find see the tape drive but fastback plus cannot too many tape read errors although not know what causing this problem discovered that using different floppy controller solves few months ago upgraded motherboard which contained integrated floppy controller already had floppy controller the 1542 initially disabled the motherboard floppy controller after while decided try disabling the 1542 floppy controller and using the one the motherboard when did this the tape drive cms jumbo 250 reliability increased dramatically and fastback plus was suddenly able find and use the tape drive don know this was caused hardware problem 1542 the one hand the floppy drives worked great when they were attached the 1542 which seems say that there was nothing wrong with the 1542 the other hand the tape drive didn work well attached the 1542 floppy controller but did work when attached different controller this could indication hardware problem 1542 did change floppy drive cables and conceivable that the problem was the cables don know what the cause really however you having similar problems you might want consider trying new floppy controller sound cards many popular sound cards can play record digitized sound and this typically done using dma like the tape drive dma the adaptec dma can conflict with the sound card dma unlike that the tape dma this conflict usually manifests itself parity error your system crashes with parity error message what happens that data being transferred quickly the sound card and the adaptec memory refresh cannot occur quickly enough which causes parity error usually getting parity error means that there hardware problem with your system this case however the parity error not symptom bad hardware found that such parity errors typically occur while recording digitized sound and the chances such errors increase you increase the recording fidelity higher sampling rate recording stereo recording using bits instead etc like the tape drive solution the solution here lower the adaptec bus timing see the section tape drives for information how this done note however that this may may not solve the problem may only reduce the probability parity error the software used record digitized sound can greatly affect this problem some software inefficient disk caches the speed your hard disk and the amount disk fragmentation can also affect this miscellaneous info this section contains miscellaneous hints tips and rumors much merely information that heard read about and have not verified believe that the following information correct but not sure use your own risk with qemm and you need specify the parameter unless you are using the aspi4dos driver you don qemm will crash hang bootup although the qemm manual mentions this the install program does not seem detect that 1542 present and automatically add this option the qemm command line least this occurred with the qemm install program haven tested any other version earlier versions qemm probably need this parameter but not sure never used version earlier than you use aspi4dos you not need give qemm the parameter some all versions the 1542 not support hard disks over one gigabyte size support hard disks with capacities over 1gb you need get new rom bios from adaptec not sure this still true the latest 1542bs being sold adaptec connect cdrom drive the 1542 you need scsi cdrom drive and some drivers note that some cdrom drives have proprietary interfaces non scsi these drives cannot used with the 1542 you have three choices for cdrom drivers have idea how well the following solutions work even they work the following secondhand information you can buy adaptec scsi driver package which lists for something like you already have older adaptec drivers you can supposedly upgrade scsi for around contact adaptec for details the scsi package supposedly contains everything that you need you can buy the corelscsi driver package which made the same people that make coreldraw this package contains cdrom drivers scsi tape drivers worm drivers etc not know the list price but seen this package sold for around note that corelscsi does not come with the aspi4dos driver which needed you not already have aspi4dos you may better off getting adaptec scsi instead this method obsolete the following drivers have been obsoleted adaptec scsi kit but mentioning case someone already has these drivers you can use the drivers the adaptec asw 1410 kit aspi4dos and the asw 410 kit aspi cdrom drivers you will have get copy mscdex exe high level cdrom driver not included the asw 410 kit but this available from several bulletin boards use scsi tape drive with the 1542 you need software that knows how talk scsi tape drive software that heard about are again like the above section cdrom drives have idea how well the following solutions work even they work the following secondhand information central point tools for msdos supposedly supports large number scsi tape drives comes with scsi drivers aspi4dos well central point backup the corelscsi driver package contains scsi tape backup program see the above section cdrom drives for more details however note that corelscsi does not come with but requires aspi4dos seen advertisements that sell the 1542 three configurations 1542 scsi controller with hard disk rom bios 1542 scsi controller bios and adaptec aspi drivers 1542 scsi controller bios adaptec aspi drivers and corelscsi drivers programs imagine that adaptec now sells the 1542 fourth configuration 1542 scsi controller bios and scsi drivers including aspi drivers those people who use unix might interested version gnu tar for msdos that talks scsi tape drive via the aspi4dos driver you need this driver before you can use this program never used this version gnu tar but heard that works don know how well though you have anonymous ftp access the internet copy can found wsmr simtel20 army mil and mirror sites pd1 msdos dskutl aspibin zip 67841 920131 gnu tar for scsi tape drives adaptec 154xx aspipat zip 21206 920131 patches for aspibin relative gnu tar aspisrc zip 221370 920131 src for gnu tar for scsi tape adaptec ctrlr have idea copy can found compuserve unixforum might have any forum does far msdos concerned the 1542a and the 1542b controllers are the same with msdos the 1542a should work well the 1542b however the hardware for these two boards not 100 identical and there least one non msdos program that initially did not work with 1542a but did work with 1542b bsd386 386 version bsd unix case anyone curious here edited copy config sys file files buffers break stacks 256 device sys dev aspi4dos sys device qemm qemm386 sys ram rom dma f800 ffff dos high umb devicehigh sys dev nnansi sys devicehigh dos setver exe shell dos command com note that using qemm and aspi4dos were using aspi4dos probably have use config sys that looked like files buffers break stacks 256 device sys