9 |text from dagibbs quantum qnx com david gibbs subject wanted advice for new cylist organization qnx software systems ltd lines article c5r7ey 7mq srgenprp com blaisec com blaise cirelli writes the question have how dangerous riding tough question more dangerous than driving car and far more dangerous you don apply modicum intelligence the activity basically stupidity will get you hurt killed lot faster motorcycle than car but with care not unreasonably dangerous also buying good protective clothing helpful that way something does wrong you are likely less severely injured first thing possible take msf driver training course this will get you started the right foot they teach control the vehicle and safe riding practices second buy protective gear minimum good helmet and pair leather gloves are must good sturdy piece footgear also very helpful though leather hiking boots pair old army boots something similar works fine for this purpose long you make sure the laces stay tied after those leather jacket and leather pants chaps are nice well but these are also expensive items for the pants many people consider good pair jeans reasonable preferably recent and fairly heavy weight similarly for jacket good jean jacket reasonable compromise though more people tend have leather jackets around than pants another thing drop garage sales looking for second hand leather jacket look for fairly thick leather these items third don anything stupid don ride after drinking even one drink can noticeably affect you judgement and balance don ride the snow when conditions are such that black ice likely very careful riding the rain slow way down take corners gingerly brake early and gently try not ride you are sick tired taking any medication with drowsiness warnings otherwise not average shape with care you should the next question have what bike would you recommend for first time rider don want race nor want ride cross country nor want ride dirt trails probably drive back roads with occasional rides city streets and freeways the maximum can spend about 2500 looking used bike would suggest mid late japanese mid sized standard something 400 650 range would probably reasonable you are shorter lighter than average you might want low 300 400 bike possible models the suzuki series gs500 gs650 etc these are generally inline bikes generally dependable except for tendency weakness the charging system stator and regulator rectifier problems first bike was about gs650 server well the honda nighthawk series this may also known the series think honda cb450 cb650 etc this another series standard motorcycles also fairly dependable kawasaki and yamaha probably have similar bikes but don know them well for mid late 80s models the above you should able buy the bike for under 2000 leaving you money for protective clothing and insurance and licensing costs hope this helps david dagibbs qnx com
