me viscosity when hot note also that the novel behaviour multi grade oils caused additives and has been reported that with the sole exception castrol gtx 10w40 oils not retain their multi grade characteristics well over time 10w30 15w40 and 20w50 oils work very well though are quick lube places any good some adequate work but there are quite few incompetent ones out there let the buyer beware watch them while they work make sure that they don overtorque the oil drain plug and keep your hand your wallet all times are oil additives like slick tufoil any good slick and tufoil are ptfe based additives many these have come onto the market recently they are different from the moly based additives that have been around since the early ptfe the chemical name for teflon trademark owned dupont general auto manufacturers not recommend use these products most usenet responses questions these additives are favorable slight increase mpg after application smoother revving but long term results whether ptfe additives are effective after miles are debatable some manufacturers such saab claim that either the product the engine flush that preceeds application causes deterioration the oil seals and eventual leakage some bmw owners have reported death valve seals shortly after the addition slick their cars this writer has been cautioned slick dealer that slick should _not_ used japanese motors may clog the oil return passages the engine otherwise there are known reports damage caused ptfe additives the other hand there are satified slick customers the world synthetic oils really work yes but more specifically most auto manufactuers accept synthetics but disagree with the extremely long oil change intervals claimed oil manufacturers auto manufacturers recommend that you continue change oil the intervals recommended the owners manual for your car even you decide try the longer intervals least change the oil filter regular intervals synthetics get just dirty conventional oils synthetic gea