15 |text from leech unc edu jon leech subject space faq how become astronaut keywords frequently asked questions article astronaut_733694515 expires may 1993 gmt distribution world organization university north carolina chapel hill lines 313 supersedes astronaut_730956661 unc edu nntp posting host mahler unc edu archive name space astronaut last modified date how become astronaut first the short form authored henry spencer then official nasa announcement how become astronaut will assume you mean nasa astronaut since probably impossible for non russian get into the cosmonaut corps paying passengers are not professional cosmonauts and the other nations have few astronauts and fly even fewer that you better off hoping win lottery becoming shuttle pilot requires lots fast jet experience which means military flying career forget that unless you want anyway you want become shuttle mission specialist you aren citizen become one that must after that the crucial thing remember that the demand for such jobs vastly exceeds the supply nasa problem not finding qualified people but thinning the lineup down manageable length not enough qualified you must avoid being dis qualified for any reason many them principle quite irrelevant the job get specialize something that involves getting your hands dirty with equipment not just paper and pencil forget computer programming entirely will done from the ground for the fore seeable future degree one field plus work experience another seems frequent winner good physical condition with good eyesight not get radial keratomy similar hack improve your vision nobody knows what sudden pressure changes would rked eyes and long term effects are poorly understood for that matter avoid any other significant medical unknowns you can pass jet pilot physical you should okay you can your chances are poor practise public speaking and conservative and conformist appearance and actions you got tough selling job ahead trying convince cautious conservative selection committee that you are better than hundreds other applicants and also that you will credit nasa after you are hired public relations significant part the job and nasa image very prim and proper the image you want squeaky clean workaholic yuppie remember also that you will need security clearance some point and security considers everybody guilty until proven innocent keep your nose clean get pilot license and make flying your number one hobby experienced pilots are known favored even for non pilot jobs work for nasa astronauts selected between 1984 and 1988 were military nasa employees and the remaining two were nasa consultant and mae jemison the first black female astronaut you apply from outside nasa and miss but they offer you job nasa take sometimes the past this has meant you look interesting but want know you bit better first think space they want highly motivated people lose chance demonstrate motivation keep trying many astronauts didn make the first time nasa national aeronautics and space administration lyndon johnson space center houston texas announcement for mission specialist and pilot astronaut candidates astronaut candidate program the national aeronautics and space administration nasa has need for pilot astronaut candidates and mission specialist astronaut candidates support the space shuttle program nasa now accepting continuous basis and plans select astronaut candidates needed persons from both the civilian sector and the military services will considered all positions are located the lyndon johnson space center houston texas and will involved year training and evaluation program space shuttle program description the numerous successful flights the space shuttle have demonstrated that operation and experimental investigations space are becoming routine the space shuttle orbiter launched into and maneuvers the earth orbit performing missions lastling days then returns earth and ready for another flight with payloads and flight crew the orbiter performs variety orbital missions including deployment and retrieval satellites service existing satellites operation specialized laboratories astronomy earth sciences materials processing manufacturing and other operations these missions will eventually include the development and servicing permanent space station the orbiter also provides staging capability for using higher orbits than can achieved the orbiter itself users the space shuttle capabilities are both domestic and foreign and include government agencies and private industries the crew normally consists five people the commander the pilot and three mission specialists occasion additional crew members are assigned the commander pilot and mission specialists are nasa astronauts pilot astronaut pilot astronauts server both space shuttle commanders and pilots during flight the commander has onboard responsibility for the vehicle crew mission success and safety flight the pilot assists the commander controlling and operating the vehicle addition the pilot may assist the deployment and retrieval satellites utilizing the remote manipulator system extra vehicular activities and other payload operations mission specialist astronaut mission specialist astronauts working with the commander and pilot have overall responsibility for the coordination shuttle operations the areas crew activity planning consumables usage and experiment and payload operations mission specialists are required have detailed knowledge shuttle systems well detailed knowledge the operational characteristics mission requirements and objectives and supporting systems and equipment for each the experiments conducted their assigned missions mission specialists will perform extra vehicular activities payload handling using the remote manipulator system and perform assist specific experimental operations astronaut candidate program basic qualification requirements applicants must meet the following minimum requirements prior submitting application mission specialist astronaut candidate bachelor degree from accredited institution engineering biological science physical science mathematics degree must followed least three years related progressively responsible professional experience advanced degree desirable and may substituted for part all the experience requirement master degree year doctoral degree years quality academic preparation important ability pass nasa class space physical which similar civilian military class flight physical and includes the following specific standards distant visual acuity 150 better uncorrected correctable each eye blood pressure 140 measured sitting position height between and inches pilot astronaut candidate bachelor degree from accredited institution engineering biological science physical science mathematics degree must followed least three years related progressively responsible professional experience advanced degree desirable quality academic preparation important least 1000 hours pilot command time jet aircraft flight test experience highly desirable ability pass nasa class space physical which similar military civilian class flight physical and includes the following specific standards distant visual acuity better uncorrected correctable each eye blood pressure 140 measured sitting position height between and inches citizenship requirements applications for the astronaut candidate program must citizens the united states note academic requirements applicants for the astronaut candidate program must meet the basic education requirements for nasa engineering and scientific positions specifically successful completion standard professional curriculum accredited college university leading least bachelor degree with major study appropriate field engineering biological science physical science mathematics the following degree fields while related engineering and the sciences are not considered qualifying degrees technology engineering technology aviation technology medical technology etc degrees psychology except for clinical psychology physiological psychology experimental psychology which are qualifying degrees nursing degrees social sciences geography anthropology archaeology etc degrees aviation aviation management similar fields application procedures civilian the application package may obtained writing nasa johnson space center astronaut selection office attn ahx houston 77058 civilian applications will accepted continuous basis when nasa decides select additional astronaut candidates consideration will given only those applications hand the date decision made applications received after that date will retained and considered for the next selection applicants will notified annually the opportunity update their applications and indicate continued interest being considered for the program those applicants who not update their applications annually will dropped from consideration and their applications will not retained after the preliminary screening applications additional information may requested for some applicants and person listed the application supervisors and references may contacted active duty military active duty military personnel must submit applications their respective military service and not directly nasa application procedures will disseminated each service selection personal interviews and thorough medical evaluations will required for both civilian and military applicants under final consideration once final selections have been made all applicants who were considered will notified the outcome the process selection rosters established through this process may used for the selection additional candidates during one year period following their establishment general program requirements selected applicants will designated astronaut candidates and will assigned the astronaut office the johnson space center houston texas the astronaut candidates will undergo year training and evaluation period during which time they will assigned technical scientific responsibilities allowing them contribute substantially ongoing programs they will also participate the basic astronaut training program which designed develop the knowledge and skills required for formal mission training upon selection for flight pilot astronaut candidates will maintain proficiency nasa aircraft during their candidate period applicants should aware that selection astronaut candidate does not insure selection astronaut final selection astronaut will depend satisfactory completion the year training and evaluation period civilian candidates who successfully complete the training and evaluation and are selected astronauts will become permanent federal employees and will expected remain with nasa for period least five years civilian candidates who are not selected astronauts may placed other positions within nasa depending upon agency requirements and manpower constraints that time successful military candidates will detailed nasa for specified tour duty nasa has affirmative action program goal having qualified minorities and women among those qualified astronaut candidates therefore qualified minorities and women are encouraged apply pay and benefits civilians salaries for civilian astronaut candidates are based the federal governments general schedule pay scales for grades through and are set accordance with each individuals academic achievements and experience other benefits include vacation and sick leave retirement plan and participation group health and life insurance plans military selected military personnel will detailed the johnson space center but will remain active duty status for pay benefits leave and other similar military matters next faq orbital and planetary launch services
