r any socially unacceptable behaviour invariably some higher authority aka absolute moral truth assuming that there absolute morality two disagreeing objectivists can either both wrong just one them right there room for compromise once you beleive absolute morals you must accept that you are amoral that everyone who disagrees with you amoral untrue one can accept that one does not know the whole truth part the objective truth about morality may well that flexibility better than rigidity compromise better than believing you have lock morals etc the same way can believe objective reality without claiming know the mechanism for quantum collapse who shot jfk objective truth that says one cannot know the objective truth interesting notion certainly one can have one morals belief that compromise good but compromise the absolute truth not something most people very successfully suppose one could hold compromise being absolute moral but then what happens when someone else insists compromise how you compromise compromising given choice between peaceful compromise endless contention say that compromise seems better and would agree but bloody pointless speak merely matter taste your liking for peace any better founded than someone else liking for ice cream looking for way say yes that question and relativism isn almost invariably when considering the relative value one thing over another morals consequences people only consider those aspects which justify desired action belief justifying commitement peace might argue that lets people live long healthy and peaceful lives while that much may well true incomplete ignoring the benefits war killing off the most agressive member society trimming down the population stimulating production the equation always more complex than presented characterize relative morals merely following one own conscience desires unduly simplify ray fischer convictions are more dangerous enemies truth ray netcom com than lies friedrich nietzsche
