3 |text from jamie zikzak apana org jamie scuglia subject workspace managers for win small review organization zikzak public access unix melbourne australia lines nntp posting host zikzak apana org thanks all those people who recommended workspace managers for windows found shareware workspace managers from australia windows archive monu6 monash edu which mirrors some sites the the three found were workspaces wspace zip this was the smallest and simplest the workspace managers that found very easy use displays small window containing buttons plus extra button for configuration purposes one annoying feature was the title window that first presented when run you must press key not mouse button for the thing away also would have been nice there was always top setting for the little window containing the workspace buttons maybe some user specified strings the buttons instead the numbers one six might nice feature the simplicity and ease use this workspace manager makes attractive package workshift wrksft16 zip while this workspace manager offered few features that workspaces lacked was quite time consuming set things with workspaces all but the first workspace initially empty with workshift you need take snapshots how you want each your workspaces look like what applications they contain also the main window quite large but this does allow you have small view what each workspace with workspaces there was facility for viewing what was workspace without switching workshift provides this viewing functionality which quite useful bigdesk and backmenu backdesk zip this interesting package which contains few other goodies well workspace manager other goodies include backmenu which provides pop root menu when you press certain mouse button just like windows the menu totally configurable offering unlimited depth cascading menus which provides quite handy access applications you could say menu based alternative the program manager also bundled backdesk zip program called wrun which allows you run windows applications from dos shell under windows instead using the file manager run applications the actual workspace manager called bigdesk bigdesk works quite differently the other two workspace managers that doesn provide certain number disjoint and separate workspaces fact basically enlarges your desktop configurable amount and you choose which region the desktop you want your screen focus this means you can have windows overlapping between different viewing regions unlike the first two workspace managers which each workspace was isolated from the other one the bigdesk control window allows move windows around your enlarged desktop basically the control window provides small scale view your viewing area while your actual computer screen provides large scale blow particular section try each them out for yourself was impressed with all them find out which one suits your needs the best
