erminology the literature for very small set concepts when algorithm depends key which isn published call private algorithm otherwise call public algorithm have encryption functions and decryption functions that for any message also have hashing functions and verification functions such that and only public key cryptosystem has public encryption and private decryption checksums such the application mentioned the previous question have public hashing and public verification digital signature functions have private hashing and public verification only one person can produce the hash for message but everyone can verify that the hash correct obviously when algorithm depends private key meant unusable anyone who doesn have the key there real difference between shared key and private key shared key isn published private you encrypt data for friend rather than for your eyes only are you suddenly doing shared key encryption rather than private key encryption what are md4 and md5 md4 and md5 are message digest functions developed ron rivest definitions appear rfc 1320 and rfc 1321 see part code available from ftpmd note that transcription error was found the original md5 draft rfc the corrected algorithm should called md5a though some people refer md5 what snefru snefru family message digest functions developed ralph merkle snefru round function the newest the family definitions appear merkle paper me91a code available from ftpsf
