en though swear that whats happening here are some relevent quotes from the manual data transferred from the disk the read buffer rate maximum 87mb minimum calculations show 3121kb sec maximum and 1578kb sec minimum disk spins 4306 rpm with sectors per track the outside and the inside single burst errors bits within one sector can corrected the fly real time they occur allowing high degree data integrity with impact the drive performance take this mean error correction isn the bottleneck for page mode operations the data transfer rate and from the buffer ram this high transfer rate allows the interface communicate over the bus data transfer rate while the dcs simultaneously controls disk ram transfers the thing can even cache pre fetch while sending the requested sector has 64kb read buffers for pre fetching guess you could call that cache when sequential read the outer tracks why getting measly 862kb sec when should getting around 3mb sec any you hard disk engineers out there know wondering why disks are slow david ooo ooo david stam linux the choice gnu generation stam netcom com 386 x11r5 openlook gcc tex free
