2 |text from rowlands pocomoco nosubdomain nodomain jon rowlands subject more gray levels out the screen nntp posting host pocomoco com reply rowlands com jon rowlands organization texas instruments spdc dsp technology branch dallas lines article 1pp991 t63 tut jk87377 lehtori tut kouhia juhana writes article 1993apr5 040819 14943 kpc com hollasch kpc com steve hollasch writes think you proposal would work get extra one maybe two extra bits color resolution however you had display that chould only zero full intensity for each primary don think you get great equivalent bit photographs have not suggested wrote about problems and the problem were clearly visible with bit images not mention bit images description experiment deleted the bit images are viewed quickly and sync with screen then 100 intensities could better than have dunno more deleted any case getting black color with slow machines problem could try our bit screens but don know how render pixels with constant time recall our double buffer has other image color and one that doesn help either maybe should dump photos screen with low level code how few years ago friend and took some 256 grey level photos from bit mac plus screen using this method displaying all 256 levels synchronized the 60hz display took about seconds after experimenting with different aperture settings and screen brightnesses found range that worked well giving respectable contrast the quality the images was pretty good there were visible contrast bands minimize the exposure time the display program built 255 different bit frames the first contained dot only for pixels that had value 255 the second only for pixels that had value 254 etc these frames were stored using sparse data structure that was very fast onto the screen sequence creating these frames sometimes took minutes that old mac but the camera shutter was closed during that time anyway and yes wrote directly the screen memory mea culpa our biggest problem was that small images were displayed the top left corner the screen instead the center took extra week have the film developed and printed because the processors took the trouble manually move the all images into the center the print who have guessed regards jon rowlands
