15 |text from jbh55289 uxa cso uiuc edu josh hopkins subject trajectory simulation keywords ssto delta clipper organization university illinois urbana lines been three talks the last month which might interest transcribed some notes below since note taking ability means infallible please assume that all factual errors are mine permission granted copy this without restriction note for newbies the delta clipper project geared towards producing single staget orbit reusable launch vehicle the vehicle scale vehicle designed test some the concepts invovled ssto currently undergoing tests the vehicle would full scale experimental vehicle capable reaching orbit has not yet been funded april 6th rocky nelson macdonnell douglas gave talk entitled optimizing techniques for advanced space missions here the university illinois nelson job involves using software simulate trajectories and determine the optimal trajectory within given requirements although not directly involved with the delta clipper project has spent time with them recently using his software for their applications thus used the project for most his examples while don think the details implicit trajectory simulation are much interest the readers hope they aren fell asleep during that part think that many you will interested some the details gleaned from the examples the first example given was the maximization payload for polar orbit the main restriction that acceleration must remain below assume that this driven passenger constraints rather than hardware constraints but did not verify that the delta clipper version has engines boosters and sustainers the boosters which have lower isp are shut down mid flight thus one critical question when shut them down nelson showed the following plot acceleration time ______ ascii graphs this actually fairly good the big difference that the lines made the should curves which are concave the data only approximate the graph wasn for very long 100 sec 400 sec mentioned before critical constraint that levels must kept below initially all eight engines are started the vehicle burns fuel the accelleration increases gets close the booster engines are throtled back however they quickly become inefficient low power soon makes more sense cut them off altogether this causes the dip accelleration about 100 seconds eventually the remaining sustainer engines bring the level back about and then hold there until they cut out entirely the engine cutoff does not acutally occur orbit the trajectory aimed for altitude slightly higher than the 100nm desired and the last vestiges air drag slow the vehicle slightly thus lowering the final altitude that desired questions from the audience paraphrased would make sense shut down the booster engines pairs rather than all once very perceptive worth considering they have not yet done the simulation shutting down all four was part the problem given what was the final payload for this trajectory can tell read aviation leak also apparently had good propulsion example but was told not use question does anyone know this security due sdio protecting national security protecting their own interests the second example was reentry simulation from orbit just before the pitch maneuver the biggest constraint this one aerodynamic heating and the parameter they were trying maximize was crossrange showed graphs heating using two different models show that both were very similar and think were supposed assume that this meant they were very accurate the end result was that for polar orbit landing ksc the would have about degrees crossrange and would start reentry profile about degrees south latitude would have asked about the landing maneuvers but didn know about that aspect the flight profile josh hopkins jbh55289 uxa cso uiuc edu find way make one attributed hannibal
