parties regardless the mobility the target the fbi investigation and without degradation service under the proposal the department justice doj can keep communications products off the market determines that these products not meet the doj own guidelines this could result increased costs and reduced competitiveness for service providers and equipment manufacturers since they will unlikely add any features that may result doj rejection their entire product the fbi proposal suggests that the cost this wiretapping service the bureau would have borne the service provider itself the electronic frontier foundation organized broad coalition public interest and industry groups from computer professionals for social responsibilty cpsr and the aclu and sun microsystems oppose the legislation white paper produced the eff and ratified the coalition entitled analysis the fbi digital telephony proposal was widely distributed throughout the congress the justice department lobbied hard the final days get congress take the bill before congress adjourned but the bill never found congressional sponsor and was therefore never officially introduced the fbi may reintroduce digital telephony when the 103rd congress convenes january ftp eff org pub eff legislation fbi wiretap bill pub eff legislation new fbi wiretap bill bill ensure the continuing access law enforcement the content wire and electronic communications when authorized law and for other purposes version the bill after fbi changes response public response pub cud law hr3515 house rep bill 3515 telecommunications law commentary pub eff papers eff fbi analysis the eff sponsored analysis the fbi digital telephony proposal pub eff papers ecpa layman the electronic communications privacy act 1986 layman view pub eff papers nightline wire transcript abc nightline may 1992 the fbi privacy and proposed wire tapping legislation featured are marc rotenberg the cpsr and william sessions director the fbi pub eff papers edwards_letter letter