12 |text from grady netcom com 1016 2ef221 subject declassifying media organization capriccioso newsreader tin version pl6 lines there are many urban legends maybe this ought the crypt faq about what actually sufficient clear declassify magnetic media when used for classified data here some information from the horse mouth regarding the sufficient overwriting media clearing meant retained within the controlled environment declassifying the material reused outside the controlled environment from national telecommunications and information systems security ntiss advisory memorandum office automation security guidelines ntissam compusec clearing magnetic media certain types removable media magnetic tape floppy disk cassettes and magnetic cards may cleared overwriting the entire media one time with any one character floppy disks may cleared applying vendor formatting program that overwrites each location with given character fixed media winchester disks should cleared overwriting least one time with any one character one way this applying vendor supplied formatting program that overwrites each location the disk with given character can shown that this program actually works advertised the user should beware some programs that purport overwrite all locations not actually this cleared media may resides within the controlled facility released for destruction however they should marked and controlled the level the most restrictive sensitivity information ever recorded declassification magnetic media certain types removable media can declassified using degaussing device that has been approved for declassifying media that type list approved devices maintained the nsa fixed medium for example hard winchester disk operative approved method declassifying the disk pack employ overwrite procedure which must overwrite all addressable locations least three times writing any character then its complement binary ones and binary zeros alternatively when fixed media become inoperative impossible declassify the media the overwrite method this case there are two alternate procedures that may used disassemble the disk pack and degauss each platter with the appropriate approved degaussing equipment and courier the inoperative media the vendor facility have the magnetic media disk platter removed sight the courier and returned the courier for destruction the secure site the vendor can then install new platters and repair any other problems with the disk unit destruction magnetic media see dod computer security center department defense magnetic remanence security guideline csc std 003 for official use only this and many other interesting documents many that are more informative than probably intended computer security procedures can obtained free from executive secretary national telecommunications and informations systems security committee national security agency fort george meade 20755 6000 write them fun the nsa mailing list grady netcom com 2ef221
