nd the chord the wings the imaginary line between the leading edge and the trailing edge slightly negative angle negative alpha this causes little bit downward force toward the belly the orbiter the direction and this force alleviates structural loading have careful about those wings they about the most delicate part the vehicle the new attitude after the roll also allows carry more mass orbit achieve higher orbit with the same mass change the orbit higher lower inclination than would the case didn roll performance gain the new attitude allows the crew fly less complicated flight path they had execute one the more dangerous abort maneuvers the return launch site decreased abort maneuver complexity the new attitude improves the ability for ground based radio antennae have good line sight signal with the band radio antennae the orbiter improved band look angles the new attitude allows the crew see the horizon which helpful but not mandatory part piloting any flying machine the new attitude orients the shuttle that the body more nearly parallel with the ground and the nose the east usually this allows the thrust from the engines add velocity the correct direction eventually achieve orbit remember velocity vector quantity made both speed and direction the shuttle has have large horizontal component its velocity and very small vertical component attain orbit this all begs the question why isn the launch pad oriented give this nice attitude begin with why does the shuttle need roll achieve that attitude the answer that the pads were leftovers from the apollo days the shuttle straddles two flame trenches one for the solid rocket motor exhaust one for the space shuttle main engine exhaust you can see the effects this any daytime launch the srm exhaust dirty gray garbage and the ssme exhaust fluffy white steam watch for the difference between the top orbiter side and the bottom external tank side the stack the access tower and other support and service structure are all orie