ng term professional relationships with their japanese counterparts program design fulfill the objectives the program participants will required develop advanced language capability and deep understanding japan and its culture correspondingly jstmp consists three major components training the japanese language several japanese language courses will offered including intensive courses designed expedite language preparation for scientists and engineers relatively short time education japanese business and social culture particular enphasis placed attaining deep understanding the cultural and educational basis japanese management approaches manufacturing and information technology courses will available variety departments throughout both universities including anthropology sociology history and political science moreover seminars and colloquiums will conducted further field trip japanese manufacturing research facilities the united states will scheduled internship study mission japan upon completion their language and cultural training pitt and cmu participants will have the opportunity japan and observe and participate the management technology internships japan will generally run for one year however shorter ones are possible fellowships covering tuition for language and culture courses well stipends for living expenses are available for more information and application materials contact steven brener susie brown jstmp carnegie mellon university gsia university pittsburgh pittsburgh 15213 3890 4e25 forbes quadrangle telephone 412 268 7806 pittsburgh 15260 fax 412 268 8163 telephone 412 648 7414 fax 412 648 2199 interested individuals companies and institutions should respond phone mail please not inquire via mail please note that this directed grads and professionals however advanced undergrads will considered further funding resticted citizens and permanent residents the steve brener
