then the resource quark compared against the quarks for the fixed strings representing the enumerated values there are many enumerated strings the converter many converters each with small number enumeration strings then global initialization routine might used turn all the resource strings into quarks that way the first time one these converters used the strings will turned into quarks and held static variables for use the next invocation one the converters data type string this type converter slightly easier than the string data type converters since the use quarks isn necessary instead the data type value simply converted string value probably the use sprintf data type string converters are useful for applications that wish convert internal data type value into string that they can write out valid resource specification file this mechanism can used provide snapshot application state into file this snapshot can used restore the program known state via the usual resource database mechanisms you are taking the trouble write string data type converter isn much extra effort write the data type string converter writing both the same time helps ensure that they are consistent iii data type data type this type converter used convert existing data type value another data type for instance pixel value can converted rgb data type that contains separate fields for red green and blue the type signature for resource converter follows typedef boolean xttypeconverter display xrmvalueptr cardinal xrmvalueptr xrmvalueptr xtpointer display dpy xrmvalueptr args cardinal num_args xrmvalueptr fromval xrmvalueptr toval xtpointer converter_data when the converter invoked the fromval argument points the source resource manager value and the toval argument points the destination resource manager value the converter_data argument opaque pointer some converter specific data that specified when the converter registered the args and num_args arguments allow extra information passed the converter when invoked for instance the pixel rgb structure converter discussed above would need colormap and visual arguments which lookup the pixel obtain the rgb values corresponding that pixel care must taken with the toval argument xrmvalue has the following type definition and specifies size and location for converted value typedef struct unsigned int size caddr_t addr xrmvalue xrmvalueptr when the converter invoked the address may point location the given size for the converted value the location can null the former case the converter should ensure that the size the destination area large enough handle the converted value the destination area not large enough then the converter should set the size the amount space needed and return false the caller can then ensure that enough space allocated and reinvoke the converter the size large enough then the converter can simply copy the converted value into the space given and return true the location null then the converter can assign the location the address static variable containing the converted value and return true when writing group converters this code often repeated and becomes convenient define macro define done var type toval addr toval size sizeof type toval size sizeof type return false else type toval addr var else toval addr caddr_t var toval size sizeof type return true define donestr str toval addr toval size sizeof string toval size sizeof string return false else toval addr caddr_t str toval size sizeof string return true inside the converter good idea perform little safety checking the num_args and args arguments ensure that your converter being called properly once you have written your converter you need register with the intrinsics the intrinsics invokes resource converters when creating widgets and fetching their resource values from the resource database register converter with single application context use xtappsettypeconverter void xtappsettypeconverter context from converter args num_args cache