b pext converters how open multiple displays see multi user application software using the resource issue summer 1992 oliver jones for complete coverage the issues involved most this answer based that article nutshell one uses xtopendisplay add each display _single_ application context and then xtclosedisplay shutdown each display and remove from the application context the real problems occur when trying close down display this can happen ways user selects quit button one the displays user has window manager send wm_delete_window message server disconnect possibly from killclient message server shutdown crash network failure assume you can deal gracefully with since _merely_ problem translating widget display and removing that display not then read the oliver jones article the third one difficult handle the following based the oliver jones article and include here because difficult problem the difficulty arises because the xlib design presumed that error always unrecoverable and fatal this essentially true for single display based application but not true for multiple display program application that does things other than display information server when error occurs the error handler called and _if_ returns then exit happens the only way around this use setjmp longjmp avoid returning the error handler the following code fragment demonstrates this include setjmp jmp_buf xiorecover void xiohandler dpy display dpy destroydisplay dpy longjmp xiorecover main setjmp xiorecover xsetioerrorhandler xiohandler xtappmainloop app_context the destroydisplay something that given display pointer can back the application specific data and perform any necessary cleanup should also call xtclosedisplay for those you unfamiliar with setjmp longjmp when setjmp first called returns and save enough information the jmp_buf that latter execution longjmp can return the program the same state the setjmp was just executed the return value this second setjmp the value the second argument longjmp there are several caveats about using these but for this purpose adequate some other problems you might run into are resource converters that improperly cache resources the most likely symptoms are xlib errors such badcolor badatom badfont there may problems with the total number displays you can open since typically only limited number file descriptors are available with being typical value you may also run into authorization problems when trying connect display there was much discussion comp windows about this topic november robert scheifler posted article which basically said this the way will and xlib will not change what changed from this addresses only changes the intrinsics first the general changes for each release are described then certainly incomplete list new functions added and others that are now deprecated are listed brevity primary goal much the following information retrieved from chapter the mit intrinsics manual and from reilly volume 3rd edition from addition gadgets windowless widgets new resource type converter interface handle cacheing and additional data variable argument list interface define xtspecificationrelease added with this release wmshellpart toplevelshellpart transientshellpart changed incompatibly core initialize core set_values added arglist and count parameters event handlers had continue_to_dispatch parameter added core set_values_almost specification changed core compress_exposure changed enumerated data type from boolean core class_inited changed enumerated data type from boolean constraint get_values_hook added extension record core initialize_hook obsolete info passed core initialize shell root_geometry_manager added extension record core set_values_hook obsolete info passed core set_values calling xtquerygeometry must store complete geometry added unrealizecallback xttranslatecoords actually works under from psuedo resource basetranslation added searching for app default and other files made more flexible customization 