trinsics are quite flexible how this file found read the next part that describes the various environment variables and how they effect where this file found thanks oliver jones pictel com for the following you can use several environment variables control how resources are loaded for your based programs xfilesearchpath xuserfilesearchpath and xapplresdir these environment variables control where looks for application defaults files application initializing loads most one app defaults file from the path defined xfilesearchpath and another from the path defined xuserfilesearchpath set xfilesearchpath software installed your system such way that app defaults files appear several different directory hierarchies suppose for example that you are running sun open windows and you also have some applications installed usr lib x11 app defaults you could set value like this for xfilesearchpath and would cause look app defaults files both usr lib x11 and usr openwin lib wherever your openwinhome located setenv xfilesearchpath usr lib x11 openwinhome lib the value this environment variable colon separated list pathnames the pathnames contain replacement characters follows see xtresolvepathname the value the filename parameter the application class name the value the file type this case the literal string app defaults customization resource only suffix none for app defaults language locale and codeset ja_jp euc language part the territory part the display language string the codeset part the display language string let take apart the example suppose the application class name myterm also suppose open windows installed usr openwin notice the example omits locale specific lookup usr lib x11 means usr lib x11 app defaults myterm openwinhome lib means usr openwin lib app defaults myterm the application initializes tries open both the above app defaults files the order shown soon finds one reads and uses and stops looking for others the effect this path search first usr lib x11 then usr openwin let consider another example this time let set xuserfilesearchpath looks for the file myterm the current working directory then for myterm the directory app defaults setenv xuserfilesearchpath home app defaults the first path the list expands myterm the second expands home app defaults myterm this convenient setting for debugging because follows the imake convention naming the app defaults file myterm the application source directory you can run the application from the directory which you are working and still have the resources loaded properly note when looking for app default files with xuserfilesearchpath for some bizarre reason neither the type nor file suffix defined and are useless with there another twist you may specify customization resource value for example you might run the myterm application like this myterm xrm customization color one your pathname specifications had the value usr lib x11 app defaults then the expanded pathname would usr lib x11 app defaults myterm color because the substitution character takes the value the customization resource the default xfilesearchpath compiled into usr lib x11 usr lib x11 usr lib x11 usr lib x11 usr lib x11 usr lib x11 note some sites replace usr lib x11 with projectroot this batch default settings the default xuserfilesearchpath also compiled into root root root root root root root either the value xapplresdir the user home directory xapplresdir not set you set xuserfilesearchpath some value other than the default ignores xapplresdir altogether notice that the quick and dirty way making your application find your app defaults file your current working directory set xapplresdir single dot all this machinery worked differently for compatibilty many people set their xapplresdir value dot followed slash what order are callbacks executed courtesy donna converse converse expo lcs mit edu the intrinsics library not guarantee order this because both the widget writer and the application writer have the ability modify the entire contents the callback list neither one currently knows what the other doing and the intrinsics cannot guarantee the order execution the application programmer cannot rely the widget writer the widget writer not required document when the widget will add and remove callbacks from the list what effect this will have therefore the functionality contained callback should independent the functionality contained other callbacks the list even though the standard the definition xtaddcallback says callback_name specifies the callback list which the procedure appended you may not infer from the word appended that the callback routines are called the same order they have been added the callback list how know widget visible courtesy donna converse converse expo lcs mit edu building widget needs know visible set the visible interest field core and window completely obscured the core visible flag goes false however window iconified the flag stays set true right everything implemented correctly this demonstrates deficiency the protocol and the core widget reflecting the capabilities the protocol the deficiency that the information available one way this case inconvenient way the specification accurate the second and third paragraphs section read this section carefully the visible field will not change response iconification visibilitynotify event will not received when the window goes from viewable unviewable that when the widget ancestor unmapped that when iconification occurs this the protocol deficiency visibility state and viewable state have specific meanings the protocol see the glossary your xlib and protocol reference manual this problem with mwm there something else which needs done you see this with any window manager with window manager the problem mwm what the fastest way determine window iconified application writer keep track with global boolean action routine with translations for mapnotify and unmapnotify the shell widget which contains your custom widget the custom widget writer see the map_state field returned call xgetwindowattributes these are suggestions how reparent widget xtreparentwidget you can why use xtmalloc xtfree etc unfortunately most code that calls malloc realloc calloc tends ignore the possibility returning null best handled something like ptr type malloc sizeof type ptr perror malloc xyzzy exit handle this common case the intrinsics define the functions xtmalloc xtcalloc xtnew xtnewstring and xtrealloc which all use the standard language functions malloc calloc and realloc but execute xterrormsg null value returned error handlers are not supposed return this effectively exits addition xtrealloc called with null pointer uses xtmalloc get the initial space this allows code like ptr ptr type malloc sizeof type else ptr type realloc ptr sizeof type count count written ptr xtrealloc ptr sizeof ptr count also xtfree accepts null pointer argument generally found the functions conveniant use however anytime allocating anything potentially large use the standard functions can fully recover from not enough memory errors xtnew and xtnewstring are conveniant macros for allocating structure copying string struct abc xyzzy char ptr char str abcdef xyzzy xtnew struct abc takes care type casting ptr xtnewstring str strict interpretation the intrinsics reference manual allow implementation provide functions that are not exchangable with malloc and free code such char ptr ptr xtmalloc 100 free ptr may not work personally call any implementation that did this broken and complain the vendor common error for motif programmers use xtfree string when they should really using xmstringfree how debug application first recomend getting purify from pure software this great package for tracing memory problems sun bit pricey 2750 but still recomend excuse the marketing blurb contact support pure com for more info purify inserts additional checking instructions directly into the object code produced existing compilers these instructions check every memory read and write performed the program under test and detect several types access errors such reading unitialized memory writing past malloc bounds writing freed memory purify inserts checking logic into all the code program including third party and vendor object code libraries and verifies system call interfaces addition purify tracks memory usage and identifies individual memory leaks using novel adaption garbage collection techniques purify nearly comprehensive memory access checking slows the target program down typically factor two five alternative package that isn pricey 395 for sun runs many unix and has pretty similar features the sentinel debugging environment this replaces malloc and several other library functions add additional checks contact cpcahil virtech vti com for more info next you are getting any sort xlib error you need run synchronous mode easily accomplished with the sync command line argument setting the variable xdebug with your debugger then set break point exit this will let you trace back the original xlib function being called you don run synchronous mode then the actual error may have occured any number calls xlib previously since the xlib calls are buffered and replies from the server are asynchronous next you are having trouble with window layout you can use the undocumented resource xtidentifywindows the class resource xtdebug cause the widget name identified with each window for example example xload xrm xtdebug true example xwininfo tree click new xload window will give the normal information but the widget name and class each window included this can help for checking the location and size errant widgets next you are having trouble with geometry managers you want test the way widget manages children you can try export lcs mit edu contrib libxtgeo tar this acts filter between any children and geometry manager and checks the behaviour both very clever idea the most unfortunate problem debugging callback while the application executing grab the keyboard mouse such from pulldown menu the server effectively locks and you need another machine and kill the debugger manually the server locks because the application being debugged has said one else can have access the keyboard but the application not stopped waiting because the debugger waiting for your commands unfortunately you can give them because all the input going your application which stopped the best way debug this kind problem with two machines your desk running the program under debugger other environment one machine and running the application the other possibly using command sequence like this othermachine xhost thismachine thismachine setenv display othermachine thismachine gdb application your favorite debugger this othermachine xhost thismachine thismachine gdb application gdb set environment display othermachine gdb run believe codecenter interpreter graphical debugger has method dealing with this explicitely calling the xlib functions release any grabs during breakpoints debugging widget problems requires pretty good debugging skills and knowledge how widgets work you can long way without knowing the internals particular widget but not very far without understanding how widget works judicious use conditional breakpoints and adding print statements with the debugger help great deal why don xtaddinput xtaddtimeout and xtaddworkproc work have got delicate problem with the three routines xtaddinput xtaddtimeout and xtaddworkproc the problem have that when use them application they seem not registred properly have made handy little testprogram where everything works perfect but real application nothing happens the introduction the xtapp functions obsoleted those routines see q19 for other changes and what happens they use default application context different then the one you may have created since events and timeouts are distributed per application context basis and you are using two application contexts you won get those events for example cnt toplevel xtappinitialize app class desc xtnumber desc argc argv fallback args cnt xtaddtimeout xtaddworkproc xtappmainloop app would never invoke the timeout what and how can implement drag and drop courtesy roger reynolds rogerr netcom com feb drag drop buzzword for moving data between clients intuitive fashion motif version supports drag drop capabilities openlook has supported all along the two protocols are not compatable with each other and far know they are not published wrote package called rdd which designed flexible public protocol for doing drag drop operations between clients intention was provide tool which would make easy for people support standard drag drop protocol the programs they develop and contribute sell regardless what widget set used long based the implementation based upon understanding the icccm conventions for more details read the code have heard from dozens people using rdd who like and feel that works whole lot better than motif stuff also there seem many who think that neat but are constrained use motif anyway the latest rdd and some other stuff available for ftp from netcom com pub rogerr possibly older version also available export lcs mit edu contrib pete ware ware cis ohio state edu cis dept ohio state university 614 292 7318 228 bolz hall 2036 neil ave 614 538 0965 columbus 43210
