y shadow over what should have been joyous blues locker room instead the mood was one relief and some disappointment shame let down said kevin miller one three blues score two goals brendan shanahan and bob bassen were the others there was need for letdown have kept working would have ended and everyone would happy instead lot players were happy just make the playoffs won and that all that matters said brett hull scoreless and minus for the night once got was really tough play some players didn have problem just because the score was announced our line didn quit said rich sutter who played with bassen and miller still had game play you can allow five goals like did that not right was disappointing see what was going bassen was almost frantic the bench because the blues effort somehow missed the announcement minnesota loss didn know was final said was kind looking around the bench didn realize was final for some reason the playoffs and that great but little disappointing play like did the end the letdown was precisely the reason that berry had instructed the scoreboard operators keep the minnesota detroit score off the board the score showed until first popped with detroit leading the third period the blues already led the time told them didn want see the score didn want know the score berry said felt had win the game and that the approach took minnesota took lead berry feared the pressure having win might bother the blues detroit led worried the blues might quit until the announcement the blues played splendidly shanahan got the crowd going the first period scoring his 50th the season then miller and bassen took charge late the period with the teams playing four four miller broke left wing deked defenseman roman hamrlik and beat former blues goalie pat jablonski with the rebound his own shot with seconds remaining the period then just seconds later bassen rifled long slap shot past jablonski after defenseman rick zombo intercepted tampa pass the neutral zone bassen made just seconds into the second period scoring the rebound bret hedican shot the goal gave him his first two goal game the season and reminded him special friend last year bassen befriended young oliver mulvihill who died rare form cancer age feb was thinking buddy oliver bassen said heaven now and know was watching know happy miller increased the blues lead break away goal set zombo then steve maltais broke curtis joseph shutout just seconds later making less than minute after the north stars final was announced tim bergland scored and cut the lead but shanahan scored his 51st converting pass from nelson emerson with seconds remaining the second period then was all lightning adam creighton scored seconds into the third period prompting berry rest the overworked joseph guy hebert allowed goals shawn chambers and danton cole span midway through the third period the goals chambers and cole made shanahan second goal stand the winner were there shanahan said the game was over were ______________ ____________________________________ ____________ __________ ________ _______ joe ashkar contact for the blues saint louis jca2 cec1 wustl edu ___ blues
