2 |text from lansd dgp toronto edu robert lansdale subject advice sought turning font outlines into renderable polygons organization csri university toronto distribution lines seeking some alternate solutions how turn postscript type truetype font outline into polygons that can subsequently scan converted scanline renderer have been studying the problem font conversion for few years but have never had the need implement such system well now have the opportunity write some font rendering software would like have some questions answered before jump into the deep end the main problem face how use the even odd non winding rules turn the outlines into single outline polygon renderer can handle complex polygons there need reduce the polygons simple polygons for example the letter there are two outlines the outside outline which clockwise truetype font the inside outline which counterclockwise one common solution used number rendering packages simply connect the inner outline the outer outline the point where the two outlines are closest this equivalent descibing polygon with holes the renderer will then make the appropriate hole since the interior polygon edges are the opposite direction the outside edges not want use this simplistic system since will not handle all outline fonts properly not simple matter connect the outer outline the inner outline for some fancy fonts does not properly handle the even odd non winding rules from research over the years the proper solution use trapezoid decomposition algorithm scan convert the outlines into trapezoids done the postscript and truetype font rasterizers these trapezoidal polygons can then easily and properly rendered the scanline renderer question are there any better solutions turning the outlines into polgyons other than the trapezoid decomposer not fond this solution since creates excess number polygons another question for those the know what the best algorithm create bevelled and offset curves for font outlines have dozen papers these subjects but can tell which method the best implement thanks for any pointers rob lansdale robert lansdale 416 978 6619 dynamic graphics project internet lansd dgp toronto edu computer systems research institute uucp uunet dgp toronto edu lansd university toronto bitnet lansd dgp utoronto toronto ontario m5s 1a4 canada
