e hours tracking down such shorts technical facilities where they were inducing severe hum into equipment the neutral usually bonded the ground the distribution transformer well the service entrance each dwelling this done primarily for lightning protection that induced lightning currents have short path back ground and also assure that the currents drawn shorts grounded objects like pipes draw enough current trip circuit breakers blow fuses quickly the bad side this that not all the neutral current from the dwelling goes through the neutral wire back the transformer some flows through the grounding electrode water pipe etc this may cause corrosion the pipes and possibly things like underground fuel oil tanks and may also cause measurable magnetic fields due the large loop between the hot conductors the service and the neutral current the water pipe and ground there are those who feel these fields may unhealthy don flame this just telling you where the field comes from not health effect far concerned the jury still out this note that the bonding jumper only installed the main panel not any sub distribution panels this one reason why illegal run service entrance cable with the sheath used neutral sub panel you must have seperate insulated conductor for the neutral the sheath can used this application only the grounding conductor the neutral bonded the grounding conductor the sub panel say forgetting remove the bonding screw all the grounding conductors the loads that panel will above ground with the possible problems listed above the code makes exceptions for ranges and dryers well feeds from one building another the cases the range and dryer the neutral may used the equipment ground under certain conditions instead seperate wire every time the code revised these exceptions come for review these exceptions were fact the first required safety grounds the days before ground outlets and such the appliance manufacturers don want have redesign their ranges and driers and the contractors don want have run four wire cable with four fairly heavy expensive wires place three wire the appliances question would safer with seperate neutrals the stove but the neutral current low for most burner settings since most current the 220 volt hots except some low settings the wires are large gauge and there are few reported cases injury damage far the exceptions have survived the case feeds between buildings primarily for lightning protection people doing wiring should aware what and what isn legal grounding conductor obviously the bare wire romex with ground anywhere there green wire installed such portable cord that good grounding conductor the sheath clamped connectors metal boxes legal grounding conductor the has aluminum band run under the steel sheath lower the resistance the sheath you can just cut this aluminum band off the ends you don have bond anything does its job touching every turn the sheath conduit emt thinwall tubing generally legal grounding conductor but may require bonding locknut where enters box panel particularly for larger pipes greenfield looks like big but you pull your own wires the empty sheath after you run not legal grounding conductor doesn have the aluminum band bond and the spiral steel has too much resistance and inductance you have run seperate green grounding conductor inside the greenfield wiremold also not legal grounding conductor the paint the boxes often prevents good contact and the feed the wiremold extension often from box the wall that may not well connected the first wiremold box have personally discovered cases where the entire run wiremold and the cases everything plugged into all the outlets the run were hot with 120 volts why get shock every time touch computer and the radiator here the office because there was ground wire the wiremold and one the outlets had shorted the edge the wiremold box you must run ground wire back the wiremold from the outlets least the first box the original wiring conduit etc where you can bond the wire the box with screw bnding clip whatever another issue while you should ground the green wire lug gcfi outlets when ever there place ground them legal the nec use them without ground ground available better have the protection the ground fault interrupter than protection you don install the interrupter doesn depend the ground trip desirable connect the ground available because the ground connected the interrupter will trip soon faulty device plugged whereas without the ground will not trip until someone something provides ground path for those questioning the legal use ungrounded gcfi read the nec 210 exception this the 1990 code code the city but know the rule hasn changed might renumbered though have only touched the surface concerning grounding there much more this subject but most you have fallen asleep now john john schmidt internet schmidt auvax1 adelphi edu technical director wbau phone days 212 456 4218 adelphi university evenings 516 877 6400 garden city new york 11530 fax 212 456 2424
