4 |text from yee nimios eng mcmaster paul yee subject perfect mag mx15f monitors nntp posting host nimios eng mcmaster organization communications research laboratory mcmaster university lines article 1993apr16 131036 1017 brtph560 bnr adcock bnr doug adcock writes been intently following the mag thread while waiting for mine arrive the mail there seems lot complaints about minor alignment problems with the mx15f one article contained comment that the owner called the factory and was told that his screen rotation was within spec that figure for image rotation would seem little high nec 5fg the specs call for greater than 3mm well monitor arrived last night and sure enough has very noticable barrel distortion not dramatic but there and especially noticable when the image doesn fill the entire screen the fact that worse the right side doesn help matters what trying find out these minor imperfections are the norm are most their monitors perfect don want send back and get one with the same even worse problem does the factory consider this kind thing normal and ship their monitors with less than perfect alignment can speak for mag innovision but far nec concerned they are adjusted factory spec before leaving the central usa distribution point for the eastern canadian market now here the key nec knows that the monitors adjustments are very sensitive shipping over distances with all the bumps rough handling and such and therefore expect and least theory require that the local distributor not dealer have adjusted the local service centre bull information systems toronto before sale this the correct and probably only way having any chance receiving perfect monitor the definition perfect seems depend how picky one case quite are other netters just living with these kind imperfections for one was not willing accept what considered substandard monitor and after two months wrangling and direct contact with nec finally received satisfactorily adjusted monitor not perfect imho but major improvement over what the dealer and distributor were trying convince was normal the short answer don accept these imperfections normal because for the premium one pays for the larger screen monitors one has right expect higher quality and you persistent you receive comments and opinions are mine not bnr doug adcock adcock bnr bell northern research research triangle park regards paul yee yee nimios eng mcmaster
