5 |text from subject quadra scsi problems organization apple computer inc lines attention mac quadra owners many storage industry experts have concluded that mac quadras suffer from timing irregularities deviating from the standard scsi specification this results silent corruption data when used with some devices including ultra modern devices although will not name the devices since not their fault example would sony inch without the special mac compatible firmware installed one solution sometimes disable blind writes the best knowledge there aren any problems with quadras and blind transfers trouble with blind transfers usually means the programmer screwed the tibs didn test their driver with the device question well designed tibs poll loop every point where delays 16µsec occur this usually occurs the first byte each block transfer but some devices can hiccup the middle blocks this happens the middle blind transfer there the possibility losing gaining byte depending which direction the tranfer was going anycase the scsi manager will eventually return phase error the end the transaction because out sync actual data loss would only occur the driver didn pay attention the errors coming back note that this effect not caused anything actually the scsi bus but rather the transfer loops inside the scsi manager the problem occurs when the processor bus errors trying access the scsi chip when the next byte hasn been clocked yet also note that the bus error dealt with bus error handler and doesn crash the machine clinton bauder apple computer
