3 |text from cgordon vpnet chi gordon hlavenka subject save hard disk allocation error cross linked organization vpnet public access lines 137 brad banko writes while running the quick compiler dos window under windows this evening got program has violated system integrity close all applications exit windows and restart your computer error gawd love windows there easy way restore everything working order what might some better approaches you probably want delete any damaged executables and reload them fresh data files should examined and repaired what might have caused this does the smartdrv cache make more vulnerable suspicious hard drive caches especially when they cache data writing you not stupid smartdrive caches things and windows also runs swap file which may contain data also all this pretty risky stuff environment the straightforward approach would run chkdsk with the option fix the disk and then looks like would probably have reinstall windows and few other things reasonably accurate prediction here brief description how dos stores files there are three pieces file the directory entry the fat chain and the data area you can think these sheet lined notebook paper sheet graph paper and stack 3x5 cards the directory entry notebook paper holds the file name actual size and first cluster number also holds some other information that not important right now the file allocation table fat chain graph paper tells where find the actual data each square graph paper holds number the number zero the cluster associated with this box available holds magic number either the last piece file bad unuseable spot the disk any other number tells which cluster contains the next section the file the data area 3x5 cards where the actual information stored the data area organized clusters fixed size storage doled out chunks one cluster each your case one cluster 2048 bytes cluster filled another allocated read file you first look the directory entry get the starting cluster number now you read the data from that cluster next look the fat entry for the cluster you just read this will tell you the cluster number for the next chunk the file naturally these numbers are usually sequential but they can jump around and even backwards continue reading one cluster time you walk this chain through the fat until you hit the marker which says the last cluster the file chkdsk the dos utility that checks the sanity and coherence the directories and the fat and can bludgeon most flaws into submission doesn have any intelligence you have double check anything fixes now let bit post mortem gfx vpic46 cvpic exe gfx vpic46 vpic txt gfx vpic46 video7 cfg gfx vpic46 orcpro2 cfg gfx vpic46 vga cfg game goose bird2 winmisc adv21 winadv exe allocation error size adjusted all these files have sizes according the fat which don match the size reported their directory entries chkdsk will alter the directory entries match the fat size other words the directory entry for cvpic exe may say the file 877 bytes long but chkdsk found fat chain clusters attached numbers obviously are made 316 lost allocation units found 224 chains 647168 bytes disk space would freed disk space was found which allocated the fat but not attached any directory entry chkdsk gives you the option converting these lost chains files you can then examine the files file0000 chk through file0223 chk and rename discard them you tell chkdsk _not_ convert them files then those clusters will simply marked available the fat gfx vpic46 cvpic exe cross linked allocation unit 16133 386spart par cross linked allocation unit 16133 these files are both referencing the _same_ data cluster obviously one them least must wrong interesting note that 386spart par your windows swap file fix this you should copy each cross linked file new name this will fix the cross link giving the files unique data spaces now delete the cross linked files examine the copies and try assemble them properly good luck hint missing pieces are likely found those lost chains the top 42366976 bytes total disk space 3958784 bytes hidden files 153600 bytes directories 36042752 bytes 1496 user files 1564672 bytes available disk your disk pretty close full this may the actual cause the problem perhaps windows needed expand its swapfile amount which exceeded available disk space any case the short summary that something trashed your fat there are utilities that can mirror your fat and help repair damage after something like this but you have run them _before_ the problem occurs sorry gordon hlavenka cgordon vpnet chi vote straight ticket procrastination party dec 3rd gordon hlavenka cgordon vpnet chi vote straight ticket procrastination party dec 3rd
