12 |text from crypt comments math ncsu edu subject cryptography faq other miscellany organization the crypt cabal lines 174 expires may 1993 gmt reply crypt comments math ncsu edu nntp posting host pad thai aktis com summary part the sci crypt faq other miscellany national security agency export restrictions tempest electromagnetic interference monitoring beale ciphers hoax american cryptographic association rsa public key patents last updated 1993 archive name cryptography faq part09 last modified 1993 faq for sci crypt part other miscellany this the ninth ten parts the sci crypt faq the parts are mostly independent but you should read the first part before the rest don have the time send out missing parts mail don ask notes such kah67 refer the reference list the last part the sections this faq are available via anonymous ftp rtfm mit edu pub usenet news answers cryptography faq part the cryptography faq posted the newsgroups sci crypt sci answers and news answers every days contents what the national security agency nsa what are the export regulations what tempest what are the beale ciphers and are they hoax what the american cryptogram association and how get touch rsa patented what about the voynich manuscript what the national security agency nsa the nsa the official security body the government was given its charter president truman the late and has continued research cryptology till the present the nsa known the largest employer mathematicians the world and also the largest purchaser computer hardware the world governments general have always been prime employers cryptologists the nsa probably possesses cryptographic expertise many years ahead the public state the art and can undoubtedly break many the systems used practice but for reasons national security almost all information about the nsa classified bamford book bamfd gives history the people and operations the nsa the following quote from massey mas88 highlights the difference between public and private research cryptography one regards cryptology the prerogative government one accepts that most cryptologic research will conducted behind closed doors without doubt the number workers engaged today such secret research cryptology far exceeds that those engaged open research cryptology for only about years has there fact been widespread open research cryptology there have been and will continue conflicts between these two research communities open research common quest for knowledge that depends for its vitality the open exchange ideas via conference presentations and publications scholarly journals but can government agency charged with responsibilities breaking the ciphers other nations countenance the publication cipher that cannot break can researcher good conscience publish such cipher that might undermine the effectiveness his own government code breakers one might argue that publication provably secure cipher would force all governments behave like stimson gentlemen but one must aware that open research cryptography fraught with political and ethical considerations severity than most scientific fields the wonder not that some conflicts have occurred between government agencies and open researchers cryptology but rather that these conflicts least those which are aware have been few and mild what are the export regulations nutshell there are two government agencies which control export encryption software one the bureau export administration bxa the department commerce authorized the export administration regulations ear another the office defense trade controls dtc the state department authorized the international traffic arms regulations itar rule thumb bxa which works with cocom has less stringent requirements but dtc which takes orders from nsa wants see everything first and can refuse transfer jurisdiction bxa the newsgroup misc legal computing carries many interesting discussions the laws surrounding cryptographic export what people think about those laws and many other complex issues which beyond the scope technical groups like sci crypt make sure consult your lawyer before doing anything which will get you thrown jail you are lucky your lawyer might know lawyer who has least heard the itar what tempest tempest standard for electromagnetic shielding for computer equipment was created response the discovery that information can read from computer radiation from crt quite distance and with little effort needless say encryption doesn much good the cleartext available this way what are the beale ciphers and are they hoax thanks jim gillogly for this information and john king for corrections the story pamphlet ward 1885 goes thomas jefferson beale and party adventurers accumulated huge mass treasure and buried bedford county virginia leaving three ciphers with innkeeper the ciphers describe the location contents and intended beneficiaries the treasure ward gives decryption the second cipher contents called was encrypted book cipher using the initial letters the declaration independence doi key and are unsolved many documents have been tried the key aficionados can join group that attempts solve various means with eye toward splitting the treasure the beale cypher association box 975 beaver falls 15010 you can get the ciphers from the rec puzzles faql including the line send index message netlib peregrine com and following the directions there are apparently several different versions the cipher floating around the correct version based the 1885 pamphlet says john king kingj hpcc01 corp com some believe the story hoax kruh kru88 gives long list problems with the story gillogly gil80 decrypted with the doi and found some unexpected strings including abfdefghiijklmmnohpp hammer president the beale cypher association agrees that this string couldn appear chance but feels there must explanation gwyn sci crypt expert unimpressed with this string what the american cryptogram association and how get touch the aca organization devoted cryptography with emphasis cryptanalysis systems that can attacked either with pencil and paper computers its organ the cryptogram includes articles and challenge ciphers among the more than cipher types english and other languages are simple substitution playfair vigenere bifid bazeries grille homophonic and cryptarithm dues are for one year issues more outside north america less for students under and seniors subscriptions should sent aca treasurer 18789 west hickory mundelein 60060 rsa patented yes the patent number 405 829 filed granted for further discussion this patent whether should have been granted algorithm patents general and related legal and moral issues see comp patents and misc legal computing for information about the league for programming freedom see ftppf note that one the original purposes comp patents was collect questions such should rsa patented which often flooded sci crypt and other technical newsgroups into more appropriate forum what about the voynich manuscript nelson reed edu nelson minar says there mailing list the subject the address write subscribe the vms mailing list voynich request rand org the ftp archive rand org pub voynich there all sorts information about the manuscript itself course good bibliography can found the ftp site kahn the codebreakers gives good introduction
