 system free options the best option xfree86 which enhanced version x386 any other version x386 will have slower performance and will more difficult compile information how obtain xfree86 listed below x386 the port the x11 server system 386 that was done thomas roell roell sgcs com supports wide variety svga boards there are major free versions x386 based x11r4 x386 included mit x11r5 distribution you don need patch into the mit source any more x386 the current commercial offering from sgcs see below commercial options metro link 2213 mcnab road pompano beach 33069 305 970 7353 fax 305 970 7351 email sales metrolink com summary qnx svr3 svr4 012 sco unixware lynxos desqview venix isc solaris pyramid sunos ega vga svga tiga targa 8514 mach fujistu matrox microfield graphics r33020 other motif openlook xview xie imaging extension video extension audio drivers multi media sgcs snitily graphics consulting services 894 brookgrove lane cupertino 95014 800 645 5501 408 255 9665 fax 408 255 9740 email info sgcs com mips zok info summary svr3 svr4 8514 ati ultra diamond stealth svga other motif dual headed server consensys corporation 1301 pat booker universal city 78148 phone 800 388 1896 fax 416 940 2903 email info consensys com summary consensys consensys version unix system release x11r4 server support for vga svga other moolit motif x11r5 clients the santa cruz operation inc box 1900 santa cruz california 95061 408 425 7222 800 sco unix fax 408 458 4227 email info sco com summary odt odt sco unix 2v4 x11r4 server support for svga 8514 tms340x0 wd90c31 xga2 assorted local bus see sco hardware compatabilty guide for actual card vendors other motif answer software consulting box 14171 columbus ohio 43214 614 263 xlab email sales x4coher com summary coherent 1r72 greater works with any vesa compliant video note other commercial vendors including vendors describing bundled software are welcome submit summary information summary information such the above what xfree86 and where get what xfree86 xfree86 enhanced version x386 which was distributed with x11r5 this release consists many bug fixes speed improvements and other enhancements here are the highlights the enhancements the speedup package from glenn lai integral part xfree86 selectable run time via the xconfig file some speedups require et4000 based svga and others require virtual screen width 1024 the speedups suitable the configuration are selected default with high quality et4000 board vram this can yield improvement the xstones benchmark over x386 the fx386 packages from jim tsillas are included the default operating mode speedup not selected this mode now equivalent performance x386 x11r4 and approximately faster than x386 support for localconn compile time selectable for server clients both this support for both svr3 and svr4 for svr4 with the advanced compatibility package local connections from sco xsight odt clients are supported drivers for ati and trident tvga8900c and tvga9000 svga chipsets refer the files readme ati and readme trident for details about the ati and trident drivers support for compressed bitmap fonts has been added thomas eberhardt code from the contrib directory export lcs mit edu type1 font code from mit contrib tape has been included and compile time selectable there are contributed type1 fonts the contrib directory export lcs mit edu new configuration method which allows the server drivers and font renderers reconfigured from both source and binary distributions integrated support for 386bsd mach and linux monochrome version the server which will run generic vga cards now included the following key features were added with the release xfree86 they were not xfree86 the monochrome server has been enhanced bank switching available svga memory allow virtual screens 1600x1200 see the x386 manual page for more information support for the hercules mono card has been added the monochrome server and with the ability support two headed server one vga and one hercules far this has only been tested svr4 also reported work under linux svr3 shared libraries tested under isc svr3 and support for svr4 there are some special considerations consider due new usl bugs see the readme svr4 file for more information support for mice and logitech mouseman trackman some versions these devices were not previously compatible new tutorial how develop correct video card and monitor timing data written eric raymond derived from previous documentation and lot experimentation greatly improved support for international keyboards including implementation the compose key functionality found many vendor servers see the x386keybd manual page for more information the accuracy with which the server detects svga pixel clocks has been improved and the timings are now stored accuracies mhz users may want consider removing existing clocks line from their xconfig file and probing using the new server many enhancements error handling and parsing the xconfig configuration file error messages are much more informative and intuitive and more validation done there are many new options that can enabled the xconfig file see the x386 manual page for more information the format this file plus number other small things refer the changelog file the source distribution for full details also included are tutorial monitor timing eric raymond and the current x386 mode database and sample xdm configuration david wexelblat what oss are supported xfree86 supports svr4 consensys svr4 microport dell esix isc mst consensys uhc svr3 isc linux mach 386 386bsd bsd 386 not supported but should work the most active bsd 386 person greg lehey grog lemis note that esix and sco are not supported yet but anyone should feel free submit patches you are interested tackling this send mail xfree86 physics what video hardware supported this time xfree86 supports the following svga chipsets tseng et4000 tseng et3000 paradise pvga1 western digital wd90c00 wd90c10 wd90c11 these are supersets the pvga1 and use its driver genoa gvga trident tvga8900c tvga9000 ati 18800 28800 all the above are supported both 256 color and monochrome modes with the exception the ati chipsets which are only supported 256 color mode the monochrome server also supports generic vga cards using 64k video memory single bank and the hercules card the et3000 only 64k video memory supported for the monochrome server and the gvga has not been tested with more than 64k appears that some the svga card manufacturers are going non traditional mechanisms for selecting pixel clock frequencies avoid having modify the server accommodate these schemes xfree86 adds support for using external program select the pixel clock this allows programs written new mechanisms are discovered refer the readme clkprog file for information how these programs work you need write one you develop such program the xfree86 team would interested including with future xfree86 releases you are purchasing new hardware for the purpose using xfree86 suggested that you purchase et4000 based board such the orchid prodesigner iis avoid recent diamond boards xfree86 will not work with them because diamond won provide programming details fact the xfree86 project actively not supporting new diamond products long such policies remain effect contributions code will not accepted because the potential liabilities you would like see this change tell diamond about some people have asked xfree86 would work with local bus eisa video cards theoretically the means communication between the cpu and the video card irrelevant xfree86 compatibility could isa eisa local bus what should matter the chipset the video card unfortunately the developers don have lot access eisa vlb machines this largely untested theory however have yet see any reports things not working one these buses and have several reports xfree86 working fine them what about accelerated boards this time there support xfree86 for accelerated boards like the ati ultra 8514 tiga etc this support available commercial products from sgcs and metrolink for svr3 and svr4 server available for 386bsd and linux contact hasty netcom com for 386bsd jon robots for linux beta 8514 server available for linux contact martin unc edu jon robots note these servers are not part xfree86 why doesn xfree86 support color vga modes the reason that this not supported the way vga implements the color modes 256 color modes each byte frame buffer memory contains pixel but the color modes are implemented bit planes each byte frame buffer memory contains bit from each each pixels and there are four such planes the mit frame buffer code not designed deal with this vga handled color modes packing bit pixels into each byte the mit code could modified support this already may not sure but for the vga way doing things complete new frame buffer implementation required some beta testers are looking into this but nothing yet available from the project what other hardware software requirements are there obviously supported svga board and are required run efficiently 16mb memory should considered minimum the various binary releases take 40mb disk space depending the whether not supports shared libraries build from sources least 80mb free disk space will required although 120mb should considered comfortable lower bound where can get source for xfree86 source patches for the current version based x11r5 pl22 from mit are available via anonymous ftp from export lcs mit edu under contrib xfree86 ftp physics under xfree86 ftp win tue under pub xfree86 for the rest this faq these location will called ftp refer the readme file under the specified directory for information which files you need get build your distribution where can get binaries for xfree86 binaries are available via anonymous ftp from ftp physics svr4 binaries under xfree86 svr4 ftp win tue svr4 binaries under pub xfree86 svr4 ferkel ucsb edu svr4 binaries under pub svr4 xfree86 stasi bradley edu svr4 binaries under pub xfree86 svr4 blancmange utexas edu svr3 isc binaries under pub isc ftp prz berlin svr3 isc binaries under pub isc xfree86 tsx mit edu linux binaries under pub linux packages x11 agate berkeley edu 386bsd binaries under pub 386bsd ports xfree86 ftp uwm edu mach binaries under i386 ensure that you are getting xfree86 some these sites may archive older releases well each binary distribution will contain readme file that describes what files you need take from the archive and which compile time option selections were made when building the distribution what general things should know about running xfree86 installation directories the top level installation directory specified the projectroot usr x386 default variable config site def binaries include files and libraries are installed projectroot bin include lib this can changed when rebuilding from sources and can modified via symbolic links for those oss that support them this directory nonstandard and was chosen this way allow xfree86 installed alongside commercial vendor supplied implementation configuration files the xfree86 server reads configuration file xconfig startup the search path contents and syntax for this file are documented the server manpage which should consulted before asking questions determining vga dot clocks and monitor modes david wexelblat dwex mtgzfs3 att com maintains database known clock settings for vga cards and monitor settings the database installed usr x386 lib x11 etc modedb txt and the source tree under mit server ddx x386 etc this database also available from him for the latest copy and kept export lcs mit edu contrib x386 modedb which updated occasionally obtain copy this database just might have the settings you need you create new settings please send them david for inclusion the database this doesn help you the videomodes doc eric raymond file with xfree86 contains tutorials how come with these timings may helpful start with settings that almost work and use this description get them right when you send the information david wexelblat for inclusion the database note the old clock exe program not supported any more and completely unnecessary you need determine dot clock values for new board remove the clocks line from your xconfig file present and start the server the server will probe for clocks itself and print them out you can use these values put clocks line into your xconfig file which not necessary but will speed starting the server the future rebuilding reconfiguring the server from the link kit you have installed the server binary link kit possible reconfigure the drivers and font renderers the server this fully explained the readme file that available with the link kit what specific things should know about running xfree86 first all the server must installed suid root mode 4755 svr4 why won xterm run properly your kernel not built with the consem module you should define consem you environment otherwise xterm won run csh users should use setenv consem the esix console driver patch 403019 known cause keymapping problems with xfree86 recommended that this patch not installed alternatively they keymap can fixed with xmodmap svr3 make sure you look ftp readme isc that what you are running 386bsd make sure you look ftp readme 386bsd also separate 386bsd faq maintained richard murphey rich rice edu the latest version should available the file xfree86 386bsd faq the following ftp sites agate berkeley edu pub 386bsd ports xfree86 wuarchive wustl edu mirrors4 386bsd ports xfree86 grasp1 univ lyon1 pub 386bsd ports xfree86 linux you must running linux 97pl4 greater and have the gcc jump libraries installed make sure the binaries x386 x386mono xload and xterm are setuid root your kernel doesn have tcp support compiled you have run the server the default startup configuration assumes that tcp not available change the two files usr x386 bin startx and usr x386 lib x11 xdm xservers removing the argument x386 make sure dev console either link dev tty0 has the major number minor number also note that dev console not owned the user running then xconsole and xterm will not permit console output redirection xdm will properly change the owner but startx won when running xdm from local you will need provide with tty for example xdm dev console for more detailed information please read the file readme present with the distribution tsx mit edu mach make sure you look ftp readme mach what things should know for building xfree86 from source this section has been removed from the faq since fully explained ftp readme and the specific readmes please look those files for information building xfree86 vii there anything special about building clients with xfree86 bsd compatibility library lot clients make use bsd functions like bcopy etc the default configuration files are set link with libxbsd which contains emulation for bcopy bzero bcmp ffs random seed better way providing the functions include x11 xfuncs source files that call them xfuncs provides macro definitions for these terms the sysv mem functions you are linking with vendor supplied library which calls some these functions then you should link with libxbsd ansiccoptions this something that was added allow developer get rid the ansi ness defined the default ccoptions without having rewrite the entire ccoptions line for example with stock mit you see something like ccoptions ansi fwritable strings and get rid the ansi ness the developer would have put ccoptions fwritable strings his imakefile with this change you would see default ansiccoptions ansi ccoptions fwritable strings and all the developer would have put the imakefile ansiccoptions get rid the ansi ness many clients will die horrible death with ansi the effect even more dramatic practice because ccoptions actually quite complex the other issue that one must add ansiccoptions ansiccoptions passcdebugflags definition xfree86 contact information ongoing development planning and support coordinated the xfree86 